ecorpc 1.10.0012
2;2;%4Car body ID = %1 with Type = %2 or Colour = %3 is invalid.;Invalid car body data received from the PLC;Correct error in the PLC program
2;3;%4Hardware endpoint '%1' for application counter from PLC not found;Mode zone-related override is enabled but the required information on the plc interface can not be assigned;- Support information for application counter by plc on interface%CrLf%- Add hardware enpoint configured in parameter "ApplClockHWEndpoint" and resart the robot control
2;4;%4Projectfolder %1 not found;Project folder is missing;Create project folder
2;5;%4Program file %1 in project %2 not found;Teach program file not found;Create missing program
2;6;%4Project or program name for typ %1 in body assignment not parameterized;The project or program name for the specified body is empty in the body assignment table;Adapt parameterization in the type assignment table and reselect car body data record.
3;5;%4Invalid degrade request from PLC;During the change in the degrade mode, an invalid command was recognized in the control. The change into the degrade mode was not carried out.;Get in contact with control supplier.
3;7;%4More than one degrade robot requested with different robot types;More than one degrade robot requested but configuration of robot type is not equal;Change configuration of robot type, review degrade concept
3;8;%4More than one degrade robot requested with different robot start positions.;More than one degrade robot requested but configuration of robot start position is not equal;Change configuration of robot start position, review degrade concept
3;9;%4More than one degrade robot requested with different conveyor stop positions.;More than one degrade robot requested but configuration of robot conveyor stop position is not equal;Change configuration of conveyor stop position, review degrade concept
3;10;%4Start timeprogram '%1' after bell disk is removed (move robot to purge position in manual mode);MainChannel not purged;Purge main channel
6;9;%4Request fixed position program no %1 from time program and no release of drives;The requested fixed position ride cannot be started, since the number lies outside of a valid range.;Check requirements for the drive release of the robot drives. %CrLf%Acknowledge, in case of reappearance, contact controller supplier.
6;11;%4Request fixed position program no %1 and no release of drives;An attempt was made to start a fixed position ride in manual mode at the vision system while no drive release was available for the robot drives.;Check requirements for the drive release of the robot drives. %CrLf%Acknowledge, in case of reappearance, contact controller supplier.
6;12;%4Request fixed position program no %1 from motion guard sequence and no release of drives;An attempt was made during a motion guard sequence to start a fixed position while no drive release was available for the robot drives.;Check requirements for the drive release of the robot drives. %CrLf%Acknowledge, in case of reappearance, contact controller supplier.
6;13;%4Request fixed position program no %1 from brake check sequence and no release of drives;An attempt was made during a brake test sequence to start a fixed position while no drive release was available for the robot drives.;Check requirements for the drive release of the robot drives. %CrLf%Acknowledge, in case of reappearance, contact controller supplier.
10;2;%4Tracking start position %1 mm of action point %2 is outside the zone start, this is not allowed.;The configured measure of the ActionPointOffset in BCU.cfg lies in front of the zone start, this is not possible in reality.%CrLf%Error in the configuration.;Correct configuration of the ActionPointOffset of the mentioned action point in BCU.cfg and restart control.
10;3;%4Start position %1mm including the overhang value %2mm of action point %3 is before zone start, this is invalid;The configured Value of the ActionPointOffset in BCU.cfg + Overhang value from typelist is before zone start, that is impossible.;Verify configuration of the ActionPointOffset from BCU.cfg and take care about the overhang value. Restart controller afterwards.
10;4;%4Syncsignal for second conveyor received but no car body in area (min=%1mm - max=%2mm).;Second conveyor should be synchronized but no car body in configured area.;Supervise conveyor position of car body and check signal source.
10;5;%4Body has reached TrackingEndPosition but Maschine %1 is still working on it.;Body has reached the TrackingEndPosition but mentioned machine is still working on this body.;Please check and enlarge if needed the TrackingEndPosition in configuration file BCU.cfg
11;3;%4Error: init of object and lock counter still active;Another zone start signal was received by the station PLC, although the current skid/product carrier did not leave the zone start area yet.;Check parameter SKIDLENGTH in the section [StationData] in the file BCU.cfg. Check signal source of the station PLC.
11;4;%4Error: no object data from station PLC;A signal zone start was received by the station PLC without previous sending of car body data.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;4;%4Error timeout program start;An attempt was made to start a program. The movement control has not given any feedback: Motionactive or Motionerror within a configurable time.;Check whether the controller program can be loaded in the teach mode by means of the teach pendant.%CrLf%Check parameter TIMEOUTMOTIONREL in file BCU.cfg. %CrLf%If the program can be loaded in the teach mode and if the error occurs again, contact control supplier.
13;5;%4Program start and robot not in home position;An attempt was made to start an profile program and the robot was not in home position and/or it did not report any home position to the BCU.;Move robot by means of vision system or teach pendant into home position. If the robot is in home position and if the error %CrLf%occurs again, contact controller supplier.
13;6;%4Start of program was called, but robot is not in home position or in allowed fixposition with No. %1;An attempt was made to start a teach program and the robot was not in an allowed position.;Move robot in home position or in allowed position. Furthermore examine, why the robot didn't move there previously.
13;9;%4Application start not possible, program already requested;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;14;%4Level %1: Timeout program abortion for already loaded program at Fixposstart;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;15;%4Level %1 machine%2: Timeout acknowledgement start of program.;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;16;%4Level %1 cannot be deselected, because drives are not ready.;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;17;%4Level %1 HOME fixed position ride cannot be started when deselected.;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;18;%4Level %1 fixed position ride HOME was interrupted when deselected.;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;19;%4Level%1: Fixed position request prog. no. %2 but no drive release.;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
13;22;%4Program start not possible, because brush file not loaded for program no. %1, %2;An attempt was made to start a program, although the brush files were not loaded correctly.;Check brush files for current profile and create by parameterizing with 3DOnsite or copying where appropriate.
13;26;%4Machine %1 Unable to save file %2.;Rpc receives the signal for the restart from the station control while the program is running;Check the indicated path in the Explorer.
13;27;%4Machine %1 System restart could not be executed - reason %2.;Rpc receives the signal for the restart from the station control while the program is running;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
13;28;%4Machine %1 could not be started because other program still active, program was aborted.;Named machine should be started, but another program is still running.%CrLf%Maybe body gap is too small.;- Deselect machine%CrLf%- Check pitch
13;33;%4The program %1 has been canceled, because signal 'BodyinPosition' inactive;The signal 'BodyInPosition' has become inactive, while an application program is processed;The signal from the PLC 'BodyInPosition' according to the directives of the interface to provide
13;34;%4Bypass signal is forced on visualisation but machine %1 is selected.;Operator has bridged the bypass signal on visualisation without deselecting the regarding machine.;Deselect regurding machine or unbridge bypass signal.
17;2;%4Body ID out of range: %1;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
20;6;%4Car body data ID: %1 in the leader memory already available;An attempt was made to insert a car body data record with an already available BodyID. Internal error.;Internal error, check car body data in Rpc and PLC, start Rpc once again if necessary so that the car body memory is reinitialized. In case of reappearance, contact controller supplier.
20;7;%4Part detect signal received from station controller and program start position already exceeded;The synchronization of the conveyor position in the zone occurred too late.;Check parameter in the section [Partdetect] in file BCU.cfg. Check signal source in station PLC. In case of repeated appearance, contact control manufacturer.
20;8;%4Part detect signal received but no object in range ;The station PLC has received a synchronization signal and no skid/product carrrier was in the area planned for that.;Check parameter in the section [Partdetect] in file BCU.cfg. Check signal source in station PLC. In case of repeated appearance, contact control manufacturer.
20;9;%4Part detect signal received but no object in zone    ;The station PLC has received a synchronization signal and no skid/product carrrier was in the zone.;Check parameter in the section [Partdetect] in file BCU.cfg. Check signal source in station PLC. In case of repeated appearance, contact control manufacturer.
20;10;%4Part detect signal received but no release in BCU.cfg  ;The station PLC has received a synchronization signal, although no release was parameterized in BCU.cfg for that.;If a synchronization signal is supposed to be received, the parameters in the section [PartDetect] in the file BCU.cfg must be set. If no synchronization signal is supposed to be received, the signal path and the parameterization in the station PLC have to be checked.
20;11;%4Part detect signal received while program running    ;The station PLC has received a synchronization signal, although the corresponding program is already running.;Check parameter in the section [Partdetect] in file BCU.cfg. Check signal source in station PLC. In case of repeated appearance, contact control manufacturer.
22;1;%4Program number %1 of level %2 out of range or not parameterized.;The station PLC has handed over a program number which is not parameterized in the type assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the type assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;3;%4Paint number: %1 paint valve number %2 out of range or not parameterized;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which the valve number is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;4;%4Paint number: %1 paint group %2 out of range or not parameterized;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which the color group is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;6;%4Project name not available;The station PLC has handed over a color number, for which the color group is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the type assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;7;%4Paint number: %1 External paint %2 color code not available  ;No external color code could be determined for the received color number in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;8;%4Multiple component operation: Paint number: %1, component %2, components no %3 out of range;No component number for the received color number could be determined from the multi-component table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;9;%4Multiple component operation: paint no: %1, paint valve %2 number out of range or not parameterized;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which the valve number is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;10;%4Multiple component operation: paint no: %1, paint group %2 out of range or not parameterized;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which the color group is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;11;%4Multiple component operation: paint no: %1, mixture ratio %2 out of range or not parameterized ;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which the mixture ratio is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;12;%4Multiple component operation: Paint no:%1 number of components %2 out of range;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which an inadmissible number of components was detected in the multi-component table.;Check parameterization of the multi-component table. Check parameterization of the permissible number of components by means of Processbuilder.
22;13;%4Conveyor stop distance for type no %1 not available;For the received type number, no supply group number could be detected from the paint assignment table.;Check parameterization in the type assignment table and carry out download where appropriate.
22;14;%4Multiple component operation: supply group %1 for color no %2 out of range (range supply group: 0..%3) ;For the received color number, no supply group number could be detected in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;15;%4Supply group %1 for color no %2 out of range (range supply group: 0..%3)  ;For the received color number, an inadmissible value for the supply group number was detected in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
22;16;%4Maximum number of supply groups out of range (Max: %1;Control was stopped due to a fatal error!;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
22;18;%4Program number %1 is not parameterized in type list ;In the type assignment, no project name and/or no name of the program is defined for the corresponding type ;Define a project name and/or a program name for the corresponding type and ensure that a profile has been taught for this type number.
22;19;%4 Color : %1: Valve %2 and supply group %3. No external paint supply system assigned in process configuration;No external paint supply system has been assigned to the combination of the valve number and the supply group, which was transferred or determined during the transmission of a new object to paint.;- Check configuration of ExternalPaintSupply systems in config file of RPC%CrLf%- Check values of ValveNr and SupplyGroup in paint assignment table %CrLf%- Check configuration part of EcoSupplyP interface in PLC
22;20;%4Color-No.: %1 Color group 2 for second run body: %2 out of range or not parametrized;The station PLC has handed over a color number for which the color group is not parameterized in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
24;1;%4Conveyor stop: robot not in preposition ;The skid/product carrier has reached the conveyor top position and the robot is not in pre-position.%CrLf%The robot's preparation is not finished yet.%CrLf%The robot's preparation is finished and the profile program was not started yet.;Check parameterization of the conveyor top position in the type assignment table.%CrLf%Check parameterization of the start of program position in the file BCU.cfg. %CrLf%Check time programs that are involved in the color change.
24;2;%4Conveyor stop: no painting release ;The skid/product carrier has reached the conveyor top position and the preparation of the robot is not finished yet.;Check time programs that are involved in the color change.
27;1;%4Body data with identification number %1 is not available at Fifo memory.;An attempt was made to find and then to delete a data record in the car body memory with the aid of the BodyID.%CrLf%The data record could not be found. Internal control error.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
27;2;%4Identification number = 0. ;An attempt was made to delete a data record in the car body memory with the aid of the BodyID. The BodyID %CrLf%with value 0 was handed over to the element. Internal control error.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
36;1;%4Fixed position In Gunbox only possible from Over Gunbox;An attempt was made to approach the fixed position InGunbox, although the robot was not in the position AboveGunbox.;In case of command via the vision system: move robot first into the position AboveGunbox.%CrLf%In case of command from time programs and/or from profile programs: change time programs and/or teach programs.
36;3;%4Only purging position possible if robot in home position and object in zone ;An attempt was made to start a fixed position ride while a car body was in the zone. In this situation, only rides into purging position and home position are possible.;After purging & home position, only fixed position rides can be started at the vision system.%CrLf% Acknowledge.
36;4;%4Fixed position not possible because object in zone ;An attempt was made to approach another fixed position in addition to the purging or home position. This is not possible for a body in the zone. ;Convey car body out of the zone or, if there is no collision danger, start fixed position above teach pendant.
36;5;%4Fixposition only possible via home position ;An attempt was made to move from one fixed position to another fixed position without going to home position first.;Move robot into home position. Then approach desired fixed position.
36;6;%4From AboveBox only Fixpositions InBox or Home possible;An attempt was made to approach another fixed position from Abovebox. Only the fixed positions InBox and home position are possible.;Acknowledge, bring robot into fixed position Inbox or home position.
36;7;%4From InBox only Fixpositions AboveBox or Home possible;An attempt was made to approach another fixed position from inbox. Only the fixed positions AboveBox and home position are possible.;Acknowledge, bring robot into fixed position Abovebox or home position.
36;8;%4From InBox only Fixposition AboveBox possible;An attempt was made to approach another fixed position from inbox. Only the fixed position AboveBox is possible.;Acknowledge, bring robot into fixed position Abovebox.
36;11;%4From BrushClean400, only FlushDry400 or Home possible;An attempt was made to go from the fixed position BrushClean400 to another fixed position than FlushDry400 or Home;Acknowledge, move robot to FlushDry400 or Home
36;12;%4From FlushDry400, only FlushDry0 or home is possible;An attempt was made to go from the fixed position FlushDry400 to another fixed position than FlushDry0 or Home;Acknowledge, move robot to FlushDry0 or Home
36;13;%4From FlushDry0, only Home possible;An attempt was made to go from the fixed position FlushDry0 to another fixed position than Home;Acknowledge, move robot to Home
36;14;%4From BrushClean0, only BrushClean400 or Home is possible;An attempt was made to go from the fixed position BrushClean0 to another fixed position than BrushClean400 or Home;Acknowledge, move robot to BrushClean400 or Home
36;15;%4From InBox, only AboveBox, BrushClean0 or Home possible;An attempt was made to go from the fixed position InBox to another fixed position than AboveBox, BrushClean0 or Home;Acknowledge, move robot to AboveBox, BrushClean0 or Home 
36;16;%4Required position %1 is only possible from: %2  fixposition;User information;None
36;20;%4From actual fixposition %1 only the following fixpositions are possible: %2;The movement from the actual fixposition to the selected is not allowed.;Acknowledge the error.%CrLf%Select a valid fixposition.
42;1;%4Error timeout reinitializing body data ;After Clear Fifo, Rpc has requested a reinitializing of the car body data at the station PLC. No reinitializing was carried out.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
43;1;%4Program number %1 out of range or not parameterized;The station PLC has handed over a program number which is not parameterized in the type assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the type assignment table and reselect car body data record.
43;2;%4Type number %1 not available;The station PLC has received the type number: 0.;Check parameterization in the station PLC and adjust where appropriate. Reselect car body data.
43;14;%4Multiple component operation: supply group %1 for color no %2 out of range (range supply group: 0..%3);For the received color number, no supply group number could be detected in the paint assignment table.;Adapt parameterization in the paint assignment table and reselect car body data record.
43;23;%4Invalid value %1 for type=%2 out of typelist;For the mentioned car body type, the indicated measure is invalid.;Adapt parameterization in the type assignment table and reselect car body data record.
43;24;%4Invalid paint valve number: %1 from station manager;A data record was received that does not contain any valid paint valve number. In BCU.cfg, a mode is configured that needs a paint valve number in the car body data record (parameter UsePlcColorValve). ;Check the color definition table and the data flow in the controller.
43;25;%4Channels to paint not available or disabled for selected color (Nr = %1, SupplyGroup = %2);For the supply group of the selected color there are no channels to paint available or are disabled;- Enable channel for supply group (only possible in manual mode)%CrLf%- Select different color%CrLf%- Unselect atomizer->robot does not paint this body
70;1;%4Set values will not be read from EcoScreen, 'Write access' on teach pendant activated. ;Visu was deactivated from the teach pendant e.g. in the user page 'Channel overview', with the check mark 'Write access. Eco Screen will be locked'.%CrLf% ;- On the user page 'Channel overview' of the teach pendant, remove the tick 'Write access. Eco Screen will %CrLf% be locked.'
70;2;%4Channel %1 can not be selected/unselected when atomizer is selected.;The Operator tried to select or unselect a paint channel while atomizer was selected.;Unselect Atomizer or Robot, the channel will be selected or unselected automatically.
70;3;%4At least one paint channel has to be selected.;All paint channels were unselected by the HMI.;Select at least one paint channel on the HMI.
74;1;%4Blocking air switched off. For reactivation quit cleaning mode and select again.;For the blocking air, a timeout has been parameterized after this timeout has elapsed, the blocking air is switched off automatically to reduce the air consumption. %CrLf%If the parameter [BlockingAir]ActiveTime is available in the Process.cfg, the value saved there is used. If this parameter is not available, the blocking air is switched off after 60 min.;To reactivate the blocking air, it is necessary to change into another operating mode and to then switch to cleaning again.
79;1;%4Valve %1 cannot be opened because valve %2 is open.;The indicated valves must not be opened simultaneously;Activate named devices according to the lock
79;5;%4Pump %1 cannot be turned on. No pump release. ;Painting path not opened or no release for dosing drives from PLC;- Open valves and main needle in painting path%CrLf%- Check release of dosing pumps (state of atomizer in HMI)
79;6;%4%1 cannot be turned on because no speed release.;Device can only be turned on after parameterized minimum rotation speed has been reached;Use a rotation speed set value which is greater than the minimum rotation speed.
79;7;%4%1 is on but there is no pressure at the initiator %2.;Compressed air supply inadequate and/or pressure switch incorrectly set;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;8;%4Initiator %1 pressure monitoring triggered.;Control air STL valves not correctly connected and/or compressed air supply inadequate and/or pressure switch incorrectly set ;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;10;%4%1 cannot be turned on because %2 and %3 not TRUE. ;Pressure is too low to activate approach switch.;Check whether process is turned on %CrLf%- check compressed air supply 
79;11;%4Pump %1 cannot be turned on in manual mode. No pump release. ;Painting path not opened or no release for dosing drives from PLC;- Open valves and main needle in painting path%CrLf%- Check release of dosing pumps (state of atomizer in HMI)
79;14;%4Interlock of device %1 was bypassed;Interlock of a device was bridged with the required value 'OmitInterlocks'. Please be careful when using the device. Operating error may lead to a damage. ;Operate the device without bridging the interlock. 
79;15;%4Main needle(s) not released: %1;Main needle was deselected in vision system;Selected main needle in vision system
79;18;%4CO2 cooler %1 is faulty. ;CO2 cooler defective;- Check if CO2 cooler is working%CrLf%- Check feedback signal of CO2 cooler
79;19;%4%1 is on and there is no pressure at initiator %2.;Control air STL valves not correctly connected and/or compressed air supply inadequate and/or pressure switch incorrectly set ;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;20;%4Device %1 should be switched, but there is no feedback from device %2. ;Control air STL valves not correctly connected and/or compressed air supply inadequate and/or pressure switch incorrectly set ;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;21;%4Valve %1 cannot be opened because valve%2 is not activated;Valve lock active;Activate named devices according to the lock
79;23;%4Monitoring high pressure supply %1 reports over pressure (NoOverpressure = %2, InRange = %3);- Pressure not within the operating range (too high, too low)%CrLf%- wire break sensor signal%CrLf% switch wrongly parameterized;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;24;%4Monitoring high pressure supply %1 reports low pressure (NoOverpressure = %2, InRange = %3);- Pressure not within the operating range (too high, too low)%CrLf%- wire break sensor signal%CrLf% switch wrongly parameterized;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;30;%4Amount of paint in dump lines while loading exceeds limit %1;Project planning error in the time program;Adjust time program and reduce paint volume in return line
79;31;%4Solvent valves of cleaning device cannot be opened because robot is not in fixed position InBox;The solvent valves in the cleaning device may only be opened when the bell / gun is in the cleaning device. Otherwise, the solvent may splash into the booth in an uncontrolled way.;Move robot into fixed position inbox first and then open the solvent valves.
79;32;%4%1 is off, but there is pressure at the initiator %2.;Control air STL valves not correctly connected and/or compressed air supply inadequate and/or pressure switch incorrectly set ;- Check pressure (where appropriate discharge)%CrLf%- Check cabling sensor%CrLf%- Check parameterization switch
79;33;%4Maximum opening time (%1) of valve (%2) with valve (%3) exceeded;Project planning error in the time program;Correct time program
79;40;%4Valve %1 cannot be opened, because mask not docked;Valve lock active;Activate named devices according to the lock
79;41;%4Valve %1 cannot be opened, because mask docked;Valve lock active;Activate named devices according to the lock
79;42;%4Initiator %1 has no signal.;The specified initiator is not occupied.;Check specified initiator.
79;43;%4Error leakage monitoring %1;The indicated leakage monitoring sensor has found a problem.;Check whether there is any leakage and solve problem where appropriate. %CrLf% Check leakage sensor for wire breakage.
79;44;%4Error leakage monitoring %1;The indicated leakage monitoring sensor has found a problem.;Check whether there is any leakage and solve problem where appropriate. %CrLf% Check leakage sensor for wire breakage.
79;45;%4%1 could not switched on because of an invalid set value for turbine speed (set value turbine speed <=0);Device can only be turned on after parameterized minimum rotation speed has been reached;Check required value and adjust where appropriate.
79;46;%4%1: Requested turbine speed has not been reached;The requested set value for turbine speed from brushes or time programs could not be reached;1. Check if set value for turbine speed is in range fo this atomizer%CrLf%2. Check if atomizer is correctly mounted (the atomizer is flush to the flange)%CrLf%3. Check feedback of turbine speed (fiber optic) for contamination%CrLf%4. Check air supply
79;60;%4Returnline purge necessary, because of pressure release via %1;The pressure to open the membrane valve was exceeded. As a result 2K material is in return line. The return line has to be purged.;In mode automatic no action necessary. The returnline is purged automatically at the end of body. In manuel mode the according timeprogram has to be started to purge the return line.
79;2004;%4Valve %1 cannot be opened because valve %2 is opened or carriage is not docked.;An attempt is made to open a valve, although another of the mentioned valves is opened or the carriage of the linear unit is  not docked. This valve can only be opened if the other valves are closed and the linear unit ;- Close all mentioned valves%CrLf%- (purge all relevant hoses if necessary)%CrLf%- Dock linear unit%CrLf%- Reopen desired valve%CrLf%
79;2005;%4Timeout when docking or undocking the carriage.;During the docking or undocking process, a timeout error has occurred. Therefore the linear unit remained too long in a transition status.;- Check pressure supply%CrLf%- Check docking and undocking valves for pressure and wear%CrLf%- Check pressure switch for docking and undocking valves%CrLf%- Drive linear unit manually into a defined state
79;2006;%4Skid can not dock, because it is not at a valid position.;Skid is supposed to be docked. That is not possible since it is not in a valid position.;Bring linear unit into valid position:%CrLf%- Start positioning time program %CrLf%-.. 
79;2007;%4The skid cannot be undocked, because the docking interface is not clean.;An attempt is made to undock the linear unit without purging the interface before;Purge interface 
