121;200;%4When unloading brushes from the memory, an error has occurred. Information: %1, %2 ;It was attempted to remove brush files from the dynamic memory (car body has left zone, reselection in zone). Here, an error has occurred. Thus, data consistency is not given anymore.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;201;%4When loading brushes into the memory, an error has occurred. Information: %1, %2;It was attempted to load brush files into the dynamic memory (new car body in zone, reselection in zone). Here, an error has occurred. Thus, data consistency is not given anymore.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;300;%4When checking the brush files, an error has occurred. Control cannot be started. ;During control run-up, the brush files are checked depending on the parameterization. Here, an error has occurred that does not allow a reasonable operation of the installation. Data inconsistency!;Evaluate error reports and delete indicated brush files, release indicated directories, check hard disk, restart control.
121;400;%4Maximum trials exceeded to get access to the BCU. Max: %1 ;It was attempted n times (refer to max.) to receive a unit from the BCU in order to read from the station FIFO (semaphore timeout). The unit was never received, however. Internal control error.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;401;%4During the attempt to receive a unit from the BCU, an error has occurred.;It was attempted to receive a unit from the BCU in order to read from the station FIFO (semaphore error). Here, an error occurred. Internal control error.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;402;%4During the attempt to return a unit to the BCU, an error has occurred ;It was attempted to return the unit received from the BCU to the BCU (semaphore error). Here, an error occurred. Internal control error.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;500;%4Invalid operation.;It was attempted to carry out an invalid operation. Control error, bug, error by debugging.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;501;%4No free storage space in brush car body preview.;A new car body has logged in in the car body FIFO. It was attempted to load the brush data for this car body. This failed because no entry was available anymore in the brush memory. Old car bodies were possibly loaded unsuccessfully.;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;600;%4Invalid path and/or file information when downloading a brush file.;A brush file was downloaded through the HMI. The path and/or file specification of the HMI does not match the name convention, however.;Check settings at the HMI, download brush file again.
121;601;%4Invalid brush file from HMI. Download failed.;A brush file was loaded through the HMI. During the inspection, an error occurred and the brush file is invalid. It cannot be updated in the control.;Check settings at the HMI, download brush file again.
121;602;%4Error when creating a brush path. Download failed. ;A brush file was loaded through the HMI. When the target directory was created, an error occurred. Error during the access to the hard disk. Internal system error.;- Check brush file in vision system%CrLf%- Download file again %CrLf%- delete file and create new
121;603;%4Download of a brush file failed. ;A brush file was loaded through the HMI. When the INI file and/or the BIN file was copied into the target directory, an error occurred. Error during the access on the hard disk. Internal system error.;- Check brush file in vision system%CrLf%- Download file again %CrLf%- delete file and create new
121;605;%4Error new object for brush. body ID = 0 not allowed.;The BCU sent a new object to the TriggerBrush (aEvtRxNewBody) but the body ID is 0. The ID must be unequal 0, however.;Search for faulty car body, possibly reselect.
121;700;%4Invalid brush from motion. Value %1. Min: %2 Max: %3 ;An invalid brush number was defaulted by the teaching program. Error in the teaching program.;Check teach program and adapt.
121;703;%4Brush file for module %1 and paint group %2 not found.;No brush file could be found for the indicated teach-in module. File does not exist. File was not loaded.;Create file for indicated module and color group.
121;704;%4Brush file not loaded yet ;The desired brush file was not loaded into the memory yet. Loading step chain blocked or not ready yet.;Acknowledge and restart. If the error is repeated, abort the car body and order again.
121;706;%4Invalid main channel group. Value: %1 Min: %2 Max: %3.;At a function call, an invalid main channel group was delivered. Internal control error. ;Get in contact with control supplier.
121;707;%4Channel %1 cannot be reserved for painting. ;It was attempted to reserve the indicated channel for painting. This channel is already reserved by another entity, however. Painting not possible.;Acknowledge and restart. If the error is repeated, abort the car body and order again.
121;708;%4No semaphores received to reserve the for painting relevant channels ;For the painting, the channels relevant for painting must be reserved by means of the element AB_TriggerBrush. The semaphore needed for that could not be received, however.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
121;709;%4Error when returning the semaphores to the channels ;For painting, the channels relevant for painting must be reserved by means of the element AB_TriggerBrush. The semaphore needed for that could be fetched, during the return an error occurred, however;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
121;710;%4Painting cannot be started. Preparation not completed. ;With the setting of the first GUNON it was attempted to reserve the channels relevant for painting. This is not possible, however, because the task planning has reported the channels as not yet "ready prepared" (PreparationDone=FALSE);Wait until the channels have been readily prepared. If this should not happen, abort car body and order again.
121;713;%4Brush %1 cannot be written yet, because channels are still occupied. ;A SET_BRUSH was set by the teach program. The set brush cannot be written yet, however, because the necessary channels are still occupied by other processes (for example purging, loading).;- Check task execution %CrLf%- Check teach program and arrange SET_BRUSH and WAIT_PROCESS_READY correctly
121;715;%4Invalid data type for painting relevant devices.;When accessing a device relevant for painting it was found that it has a wrong data type. Allowed are BOOL, INT, DINT, REAL.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
121;716;%4Brush file for module %1 and color %2 not found.;No brush file could be found for the indicated teach-in module. File does not exist. File was not loaded.;Create file for indicated module and color.
121;719;%4Invalid data type for idle brush nominal value.;During the access to an IdleBrush required value, it was found that a wrong data type was used. INT, DINT, REAL, are allowed.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
121;720;%4Invalid nominal value for %1 in brush %2. Only even numbers allowed, found %3. ;In a required value, a REAL number was used for the mentioned brush. Only INT/DINT figures are allowed.;Check brush file, check 3DOnSite parameterization.
121;721;%4Channel %1 cannot be reserved for painting because no paint loaded. ;An attempt was made to reserve the indicated channel for painting. This channel does not have the status paint, however. Painting not possible.;Acknowledge and restart. If the error is repeated, abort the car body and order again.
121;722;%4No required values parameterized for brush %1 and paint group %2 in the module %3 ;For the indicated brush number, no required values are parameterized in the corresponding brush table.;* Parameterize missing required values and download changed brush table %CrLf%* Deactivate monitoring of missing brush required values in configuration 
121;723;%44No required values parameterized for brush %1 and paint %2 in the module %3 ;For the indicated brush number, no required values are parameterized in the corresponding brush table.;* Parameterize missing required values and download changed brush table %CrLf%* Deactivate monitoring of missing brush required values in configuration 
121;724;%4Too many devices configured for idle-brush;Processbuilder project planning error ;Check configuration in ProcessBuilder and generate code again.
121;725;%4The process for the actual object has been aborted. Application result is negative;The conditions for an error-free resume of the application after a break are no longer given. Possible causes are interventions in the process in manual mode like switching devices or starting time programs;Acknowledge fault
121;803;%4Error when generating the brush reference table. Information %1, %2 ;While creating the brush reference table, an internal control problem occurred. Data are inconsistent.;Export software with ProcessBuilder again and compile again.
121;900;%4Not possible to delete pushout-learnfile in operating mode automatic.;Not possible to delete Pushout-Learnfile in operating mode automatic.;Change operation mode. Repeat deletion.
121;1000;%4A device from the channel %1 should be triggered although the channel is not reserved.;A device in the specified channel should be triggered while application although the channel is not reserved for application.;Check teach program and adapt.
122;1;%4No dosing unit for statistics/push out found.;In configuration, no device is assigned to the painting;Check configuration and restart control.
122;3;%4Error %1 in operation %3 with HashMap.;Error in operation with HashMap.;Check corresponding code place with debugger and restart control.
122;5;%4No name for configured painting device found. ;Error or reading error of the configuration;Check configuration and restart control.
122;6;%4Error when creating the structures for PushOut. ;It was attempted to create a dynamic memory element. Here, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Cause: bug / internal control problem%CrLf%;Check corresponding code place with debugger and restart control.
122;7;%4Abort PushOut %1 due to occurrence of error ;Routines were aborted by the occurrence of an error.;Acknowledge and restart. If the error is repeated, abort the car body and order again.
122;8;%4Error %1 in operation %3 with array. ;While working with a dynamic array, this error resulted.;Check corresponding code place with debugger and restart control.
122;9;%4Error in operation %1 with file %2. Data: %3  ;During the operation with a file, the error resulted;Check corresponding code place with debugger and restart control.
122;10;%4During the saving of the learning values in a file, an error occurred. ;When saving the learning values in a file, an error occurred.;Check mentioned file and restart control
122;11;%4The general data of the painting data do not correspond to the data from the learning value file. ;In the comparison of the general data for the PushOut, a difference occurred between the stored data from the file and the current type data.;Check corresponding code place with debugger and restart control.
122;15;%4Error when creating the directory %1 ;It was attempted to create the indicated directory. This was not possible, however.%CrLf%- Target path reserved%CrLf%- System-dependent refusal of hard disk access%CrLf%- Internal error%CrLf%;Check indicated causes.
122;19;%4Error while reading learned data file.;Error when reading out a PushOut learning file.;Get in contact with control supplier.
122;20;%4The velocity override was reduced while PushOut learning cycle was active. This could cause an error while painting.;The speed is not set on 100%. This leads to a higher paint consumption, which may result in an error during PushOut.;Reset the speed override to 100 % at the KeTop again.
122;21;%4The velocity override was reduced while PushOut learning process was active. Learning cycle was aborted.;The speed is not set on 100%. This leads to a higher paint consumption, which may result in an error during PushOut.;Reset the speed override to 100 % at the KeTop again.
122;22;%4PushOut volume was exceeded. Main needle locked.;The set pushout volume was exceeded;Acknowledge and start new learning process if necessary.
122;25;%4Unexpected %1-trigger: %3. Trigger %2 was expected. PushOut aborted.;The PushOut mechanism compares the trigger.-/brush names with the names that have been saved in the reference file during learning. While comparing the actual trigger  an error occured;Send error message as well as all necessary protocols for the error analysis to controller supplier.
122;26;%4%1PushOut aborted: %2 smaller than %3;Wrong PushOut-configuration in PCA-table;1. Change PushOut-configuration in PCA-table%CrLf%2. Min-Value < Max-ValueMin-Value%CrLf%3. NextColor-PushOut > Max-Value Solvent-PushOut
122;27;%4%1Parameter %2 for PushOut not included in %3 . PushOut can not be started;Wrong or missing configuration entry with the specified data.;Check configuration and restart control.
123;5;%4No painting release from ext. paint supply while accessing system. Color valve %1 ;- No more paint in the indicated special color system anymore %CrLf%- special color system was deselected in the paint mix room;Check release of special color system and abort current processing where appropriate
123;10;%4Ext. paint supply system %1 no painting release because reflow is active. ;Project planning error in robot software.;1. Use 3DOnSite to create a logfile-collector package and send it to DÜRR-service%CrLf%2. Quitt error and try to continue.%CrLf%3. If continuing isn't possible, deselect the atmoizer and try to quitt errors again%CrLf%4. If continuing isn't possible, deselect the robot and try to quitt errors again%CrLf%5. Restart the robot control%CrLf%%CrLf%
123;11;%4Ext. paint supply system %1 no painting release because painting finished is already set on interface.;Project planning error in robot software.;1. Use 3DOnSite to create a logfile-collector package and send it to DÜRR-service%CrLf%2. Quitt error and try to continue.%CrLf%3. If continuing isn't possible, deselect the atmoizer and try to quitt errors again%CrLf%4. If continuing isn't possible, deselect the robot and try to quitt errors again%CrLf%5. Restart the robot control%CrLf%%CrLf%
123;12;%4Ext. paint supply system %1 painting release is not set on interface.;- No more paint in the indicated special color system anymore %CrLf%- special color system was deselected in the paint mix room;Check release of special color system and abort current processing where appropriate
123;13;%4Ext. paint supply system %1 no release for reflow because not all connected consumers are requesting reflow. ;Project planning error in robot software.;1. Use 3DOnSite to create a logfile-collector package and send it to DÜRR-service%CrLf%2. Quitt error and try to continue.%CrLf%3. If continuing isn't possible, deselect the atmoizer and try to quitt errors again%CrLf%4. If continuing isn't possible, deselect the robot and try to quitt errors again%CrLf%5. Restart the robot control%CrLf%%CrLf%
