130;1;%4TP '%1' can't be started, since MainChannel not purged;MainChannel not purged;Purge main channel
130;2;%4TP '%1' can't be started, because colour data in %2 and %3 are different.;During start of a time program, it turned out that the subchannels to be used had wrong color information (e.g. color code, mixture ratio etc.).;Purge the system including subchannels. Then select paint again via the primary channel.
130;3;%4TP '%1' can't be started, because the subchannels are not prepared;During start of a time program, it turned out that the subchannels to be used are not prepared.;First prepare the used subchannels.
130;4;%4TP '%1' can't be started, because channel for stock paint is not purged;Only a purged channel may be filled with paint, since otherwise soiling may be the result.;Purge channel
130;5;%4TP '%1' can't be started, because channel for hardener is not purged;Only a purged channel may be filled with paint, since otherwise soiling may be the result.;Purge channel
130;6;%4TP '%1' can't be started, because DockingUnit is not purged;DockingUnit not purged;Purge DockingUnit
130;7;%4LCC is not in the valve position of the selected color.;A new color was selected and the LCC was not positioned to the valve subsequently.;Position LCC
130;9;%4TP %1 can't be started because errors exist in the channels involved;- Errors on the channels involved;Read detailed fault messages. Acknowledge fault.
130;10;%4TP %1 can't be started because no color is selected.;A time program to load color should be started.%CrLf%The start is prevented because no valid color is selected;Select a valid color and restart the time program
130;11;%4TP %1 can't be started because the process is not turned on.;Power for process drives not connected.;- Check if "process" is enabled on the hmi, enable "process" if necessary%CrLf%- Check if "process" is switched on, switch on "process" if necessary
130;12;%4TP %1 can't be started because the drives are not turned on.;The requested fixed position ride cannot be started, since the number lies outside of a valid range.;- Check if "robot" is enabled on the hmi, enable "robot" if necessary%CrLf%- Check if drives are switched on, switch on drives if necessary
130;13;%4TP %1 can't be started because required channels are still occupied.;Time program cannot be started because a required channel is deactivated;- Check if time programs are still running and wait until they are finished or stop them manually.%CrLf%- Restart time program
130;14;%4TP %1 can't be started because the time programm was not found.;Time program not available;Check time program with 3DOnsite, create again where appropriate
130;15;%4TP '%1' can't be executed, because referencing of the color changer is active.;Referencing of color changer is active. Meanwhile, no other time program is allowed to run.;Wait until referencing has ended.
130;16;%4The main channel has a single component color selected, the time program for loading is for mixed colors;The selected time program to load the atomizer contains signals for several components (e.g stock paint and hardener). The selected color in the atomizer (main channel)  is a single component color;Check time program with 3DOnsite, create again where appropriate
130;17;%4Color data of component %1 in channel %2 doesn't match the data in the parameter tables;Properties of colors/components were changed in paint assignment table and agree not currently consistent with the data in the channels of the robot%CrLf%- Color group%CrLf%- Color number%CrLf%- Color code%CrLf%- Mix ratio;Purge the system including subchannels. Then select paint again via the primary channel.
130;18;%4Time program '%1' can only be executed in operation mode 'manual';Time program can be started only in the specified operation mode;Switch to the specified operation mode
130;19;%4Time program '%1' can only be executed in operation mode 'manual' or 'maintenance';Time program can be started only in the specified operation mode;Switch to the specified operation mode
130;20;%4Time %1 program can not be executed, because atomizer is not "loaded";The atomizer must be in state "loaded" before the time program can be executed;Run time program from group "Atomizer load"
130;50;%4Time program %1 can not be started because color changer or painting canister 1 is not purged;1. To be able to start the selected time program, the named process part has to state 'purged';1. Purge color changer e.g paint canister 1 before time program to load paint canister 1 can be executed
130;51;%4Time program %1 can not be started because color changer or painting canister 1 is not loaded;1. To be able to start the selected time program, the named process part has to be state 'color';1. Load color changer e.g. painting canister 1 before reload of painting canister 1 can be executed
130;52;%4Time program can not be started because isolation cylinder ISO1 is not in state 'Isolated line reset ready';1. To be able to start the selected time program, the isolation cylinder ISO1 has to be state 'reset';1.Execute time program to reset isolation line 1 before painting canister 1 can be reloaded
130;53;%4Time program %1 can not be started because channel %2 doesn't have the required process state %3;1. To be able to start the selected time program, the named channel has to be the requested state;1. Set notified process part to required state by executing time program
140;1;%4Required amounts of paint can not be determined because 'PushOut' function is not active or failed;The process EcoChargeC depends on the PushOut mechanism to evaluate the required paint amounts. This mechanism isn't activated or reports errors;Check if configuration parameter 'ActivatePushOut' is turned on in the group' TriggerBrush' of the process configuration (PCU1.cfg)
