152;4055;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 configured I/O assignment QW11 wrong ;Configured assignment of a local IO area to the indicated fieldbus IO area in the SPC200 is not permissible, because the local unit itself is not available.%CrLf%OR%CrLf%the field bus IO area is already occupied. ;Correct configuration, see description to the field bus unit or in the configuration menu of WinPISA from version 4.41.
152;4056;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 configured I/O assignment QW12 is wrong;Configured assignment of a local IO area to the indicated fieldbus IO area in the SPC200 is not permissible, because the local unit itself is not available.%CrLf%OR%CrLf%the field bus IO area is already occupied. ;Correct configuration, see description to the field bus unit or in the configuration menu of WinPISA from version 4.41.
152;4057;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 configured I/O assignment QW13 is wrong;Configured assignment of a local IO area to the indicated fieldbus IO area in the SPC200 is not permissible, because the local unit itself is not available.%CrLf%OR%CrLf%the field bus IO area is already occupied. ;Correct configuration, see description to the field bus unit or in the configuration menu of WinPISA from version 4.41.
152;4058;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 The AIF at the string %3 has detected undervoltage at the load voltage. ;The AIF x found undervoltage at the load voltage. The valve goes automatically into center position, the axis is not controlled anymore.;Supply load voltage again and acknowledge error
152;4059;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 A CP module of an AIF string has detected undervoltage at the load voltage;A CP module of an AIF string has detected undervoltage at the load voltage;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
152;4060;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 start program no. %3 not available.;Start program not available;Correct start program number and/or load/enter start program
152;4061;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC batch: %3 subprogram not available.;Subprogram not available.;Correct NC record and/or load/enter program
152;4062;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record %3 not available.;NC batch is not available.;Correct NC record
152;4063;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 program number identical.;Program number with L command is identical with number of the calling program;Correct NC record
152;4064;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 permissible interlacing depth exceeded;permissible nesting depth exceeded with L command;Correct NC record
152;4065;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 direct required value specification inadmissible;Direct required value specification (M10) or direct control of the valve tension (M39) active with new required value (NC command: G00, G01, G02, M10, M39);Correct NC record, only terminate direct required value specification or direct control of the valve tension with M12 
152;4066;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 Arithmetic overflow in one register;Arithmetic overflow in a register.;Correct NC record
152;4067;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 record overrun ;NC batch: batch overflow.;Finish NC programs with the command M02 and/or M30
152;4068;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 order cannot be executed ;NC command cannot be executed. Either it is not supported by the firmware or the axis specification is invalid.;Check axis specification, check firmware version
152;4069;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 transformation for this required value is already being carried out.;Transformation for this required value already occurs.;Analog required value input must be deactivated with M12 before it is reactivated with M10.
152;4070;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 The programmed required value input is not available .;The programmed required value input is not available.;Correct NC record
152;4071;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 programmed input or output is not available.;Programmed input or output is not available. Input/output address or IO module not available.;Correct NC record%CrLf%Correct input and/or output address%CrLf%
152;4072;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 register index is invalid.;Register index is invalid.;Correct NC record
152;4073;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 absolute preselection value inadmissible;The absolute preselection value (G25) in the selected register @n does not lie between the last required position or the last switching position and the new required position.;Correct NC record
152;4074;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 required value specification via field bus faulty;The required value specification via field bus (M10, channel 5) cannot be activated, since there is no field bus card or the used field bus card does not support this function.;Check type and software version of the field bus card, exchange where appropriate. %CrLf%Permissible:%CrLf%-SPC200-COM-PDP from version 2.0%CrLf%-SPC200-COM-DN2%CrLf%-SPC200-COM-CO2%CrLf% 
152;4075;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 positioning timeout;Positioning timeout:%CrLf%The reference position and/or the position of the last moving task could not be reached fast enough (MC error)%CrLf%;Remove obstacle in the traveling area and/or check supply pressure or increase positioning timeout and/or optimize regulator
152;4076;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 required position beyond the software end positions;Required position outside of the software end positions, the positioning process is not started;Correct NC record, position list or software ends
152;4077;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 inadmissible positioning order with position-dependent record relaying;Inadmissible positioning task with position-dependent record relaying (G25);Correct NC record and/or position list (refer to NC command "G25").
152;4078;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC batch: %3 demanded speed is not accessible ;demanded speed cannot be reached;Correct maximum speed or speed factor
152;4079;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 error ident ride step %3, error in precalculation of the control parameters;Error in precalculation of the control parameters (x10, x50, x90) or timeout (x20, X60, XA0);Check regulator, axis and application data
152;4080;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 error ident ride step %3, The system identification was aborted by a stop;The system identification was aborted by a stop. The stop may have been activated by the customer or by a system error.;Check I/O linking, check error stack (with WinPisa) and remove error cause where appropriate
152;4081;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 error ident ride step %3, during the system identification no reasonable parameters were found.;During system identification, no reasonable parameters were found;Check regulator, axes and application data, check limiting conditions%CrLf%- Design susceptible to vibrations?%CrLf%- supply pressure stable?%CrLf%- Is the carrier of the measuring system correctly reinforced and so forth %CrLf%
152;4082;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 error ident ride step %3, during the restoring of the original parameterization an error has occurred ;When restoring the original parameterization, an error occurred;Check regulator, axis and application data
152;4083;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 error ident ride step %3, during the initializing of the identification step, an error has occurred.;When initializing the identification step, an error occurred;Check regulator, axis and application data
152;4084;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC batch: %3 NC order G00 not possible.;NC command G00 not possible, since no dynamic identification ride was carried out yet;Carry out dynamic identification ride
152;4085;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 regulator in the SPC200 cannot be initialized ;Regulator in the SPC200 cannot be initialized;Check regulator, axis and application data
152;4086;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 for this axis a task is already active;A task is already active for this axis (positioning, identification...). A new task can only be accepted after the old one was ended.;Correct NC record and/or stop system before carrying out the action
152;4087;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC batch: %3 contents of a position register is invalid;Contents of a position register are invalid;Correct NC record
152;4088;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 violation of the stroke limit value ;Violation of the stroke limit value (M40) at M39;Check stroke limit value and valve adjusting value in the command M39, correct NC record where appropriate
152;4089;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 system identification aborted;System identification aborted since enable signal is missing;Set ENABLE input and restart identification ride 
152;4090;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 ID data invalid ;ID data invalid;Carry out system identification once again
152;4091;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 inadmissible positioning quality grade;Inadmissible positioning quality grade;Correct NC record
152;4092;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 regulator is inactive ;Regulator is inactive, since enable signal for initial startup or after movement test is missing or the configuration is faulty.%CrLf%Only with stepping motor axis:%CrLf%-No ready-signal from axis controler%CrLf%;Generate increasing flank on input ENABLE or check regulator, axis and application data%CrLf%Correct error at the stepping motor controller%CrLf%
152;4093;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 order is not supported by this axis type;Command is not supported by this axis type:%CrLf%With pneumatic axes: Command reference ride (G74)%CrLf%With electrical axes: Activate analog input in mode 0 and 1 (M10), command M39%CrLf%;Correct NC record
152;4094;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 reference position for this axis unknown;Reference position for this axis unknown;Carry out reference ride
152;4095;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 violation of the software ends;Violation of the software end positions with command M39;Check software ends and correct valve value in the command M39, correct NC program where appropriate
152;4096;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC batch: %3 violation of the speed limit value;Violation of the speed limit value (M41) at M39;Check speed limit value and correct valve value in the command M39, correct NC program where appropriate
152;4097;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 The indicated reference ride mode is not permissible for this axis.;The indicated reference ride mode is not permissible for this axis.;Correct command, check reference ride mode in the application data, compare with currently used data %CrLf%Admissible:%CrLf%- stepping motor axis: %CrLf%modes 0 to 4/ /- Pneum. axis: %CrLf%modes 0, 5 to 7/ /
152;4098;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 reference ride in mode 7 inadmissible;The reference ride was carried out for the pneumatic axis in the mode 7. For the desired command, the mode 0, 5 or 6 is necessary, however. ;Before the concerned command, carry out the reference ride in the modes 0, 5 or 6. %CrLf%In mode 7 only: %CrLf%G01, G02 and M39 are permissible, also refer to command G 74%CrLf%
152;4099;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 parameter outside of the permissible area;Parameter outside of the permissible area;Correct NC record
152;4100;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 The transferred required value is smaller than the lower software end ;Error in the digital required value specification via field bus.;Check the required values created in the field bus master (PLC) and adapt to the permissible traveling area where appropriate.%CrLf%Check limit values in the application data, adjust where appropriate.%CrLf%
152;4101;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 The transferred required value is larger than the upper software end ;Error in the digital required value specification via field bus.;Check the required values created in the field bus master (PLC) and adapt to the permissible traveling area where appropriate.%CrLf%Check limit values in the application data, adjust where appropriate.%CrLf%
152;4102;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 software end is beyond the possible traveling range ;Software end position lies outside of the possible traveling area;Correct parameter
152;4103;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 mass load is beyond the permissible area ;Mass load lies outside of the permissible area;Correct parameter
152;4104;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 amplification factor inadmissible;Amplification factor inadmissible;Correct parameter
152;4105;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 attenuation factor inadmissible ;Attenuation factor inadmissible;Correct parameter
152;4106;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 filter factor inadmissible ;Filter factor inadmissible;Correct parameter
152;4107;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 measuring system length invalid / measured value beyond the set cylinder length ;Measuring system length invalid or measured value outside of the put cylinder length;Correct parameter
152;4108;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 parameter limit infringed;Parameter limit violated;Correct parameter
152;4109;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 measuring system type inadmissible ;Measuring system type inadmissible;Correct parameter
152;4110;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 step frequency inadmissible;permissible step frequency (traveling frequency) undershot (< 80 Hz) or exceeded (> 40000 Hz);Check resolution and/or correct maximum speed
152;4111;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 adaptation data faulty;Adaptation data faulty;Carry out data reset
152;4112;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 syntax error/program number inadmissible NC/prg %3 ;Syntax error or inadmissible program number entered;Correct input
152;4113;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program %3 could not be loaded ;When using the control panel: %CrLf%Inadmissible program number selected, program cannot be created, because already available or program cannot be opened, because not available. No free storage space.%CrLf%When using WinPISA: Progr;Correct input %CrLf%If the max. number of NC records is not reached yet: %CrLf%- Carry out program modification with WinPISA, memory is rearranged where appropriate. %CrLf%- After rearrangement of the memory, load program again.
152;4114;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 NC record: %3 inadmissible record number ;Inadmissible record number;Correct input
152;4115;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 no free storage space for new program ;No free storage space for new program;Delete not required program and NC records 
152;4116;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 checksum error ;Checksum error;Service case
152;4117;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 error when uploading/downloading with WinPISA ;Error in upload/download with WinPISA;Connect cable and check diagnosis unit, use lower baud rate where appropriate
152;4118;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 enable signal is missing ;Enable signal is missing;Connect 1 signal to input ENABLE
152;4119;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 system is stopped, at the STOP input, 0 signal is supplied ;System is stopped, 0 signal is supplied to the STOP input ;Connect 1 signal to input STOP
152;4120;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 start program not available ;Start program not available;Correct number of start program
152;4121;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 order not permissible in this operating mode ;Command not permissible in this operating mode ;Do not use command in the current operating mode or change operating mode
152;4122;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 order and/or operating function inadmissible with active NC program;Command and/or operating function inadmissible with active NC program ;Stop system and call command and/or operating function once again
152;4123;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 regulator is inactive. Release signal is missing/configuration faulty;Regulator is inactive, since enable signal for initial startup is missing or configuration is faulty%CrLf%Only with stepping motor axis: no ready signal from the power activation ;Generate increasing flank on input ENABLE or check regulator, axis and application data%CrLf% Correct error at the stepping motor controller%CrLf%
152;4124;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 inadmissible NC orders used;The NC program contains new NC commands and extended NC syntax that is not supported by the control panel SPC200-MMI-1... (also refer to chapter NO TAG).;Use WinPISA from version 4.3 to edit such NC programs
152;4125;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 movement test cannot be started ENABLE not false ;Movement test cannot be run, because the input ENABLE supplies 1 signal.;Connect 0 signal to input ENABLE
152;4126;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 valve tension cannot be changed. ENABLE not true ;Valve tension cannot be changed, because the input ENABLE supplies 0 signal ;Connect 1 signal to input ENABLE
152;4127;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 movement test was aborted. ENABLE not true ;Movement test was aborted, because ENABLE supplies 0 signal.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
152;4128;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 program: %3 compatibility error between WinPISA, MMI and the operating system of the SPC200 ;Compatibility error between WinPISA, MMI and the operating system version of the SPC200. A program available in the SPC200 cannot be adapted with the used WinPISA.;Use newest WinPISA version.%CrLf%- Cancel all programs where appropriate and load again into the SPC200.%CrLf%Note: In the download area of Festo <festo.com> you will find the current WinPISA version.   
152;4130;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 too many trace variables defined. ;Too many trace variables defined. Max 10 trace variables per axis are permissible.;Check measured value configuration.
152;4131;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 trace memory reserved for other axis ;Trace memory reserved for other axis;Make default measured value configuration for all axes. After that, specify desired configuration again.
152;4132;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 unknown trace variable defined ;Unknown trace variable defined (defined by the use of different firmware versions);Make default measured value configuration for all axes. After that, specify desired configuration again.
152;4133;%4LCC %1 Axis/device: %2 trace not configured.;Trace not configured.;Carry out system reset.
154;2;%4%1: Upper warning limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;4;%4%1: Upper alarm limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;5;%4%1: Paint pressure has fallen below warning limit.;During painting, the pressure at the indicated sensor is supervised. This fell below the indicated limit. Causes for that may be missing paint supply pressure, hose break, defective paint pressure regulator or defective dosing pump.;Check indicated causes.
154;6;%4%1: Paint pressure exceeds warning limit.;During painting, the pressure at the indicated sensor is supervised. This exceeded the indicated limit. Defective dosing pump, blocked line or main needle may be causes for that.;Check indicated causes.
154;7;%4%1: Paint pressure has fallen below alarm limit.;During painting, the pressure at the indicated sensor is supervised. This fell below the indicated limit. Causes for that may be missing paint supply pressure, hose break, defective paint pressure regulator or defective dosing pump.;Check indicated causes.
154;8;%4%1: Paint pressure exceeds alarm limit.;During painting, the pressure at the indicated sensor is supervised. This exceeded the indicated limit. Defective dosing pump, blocked line or main needle may be causes for that.;Check indicated causes.
154;100;%4%1: General monitoring lower warning limit fallen below.;User information;None
154;101;%4%1: General monitoring upper warning limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;102;%4%1: General monitoring lower alarm limit fallen below.;User information;None
154;103;%4%1: General monitoring lower alarm limit fallen below.;User information;None
154;104;%4%1: General monitoring lower alarm limit fallen below.;User information;None
154;105;%4%1: General monitoring lower alarm limit fallen below.;User information;None
154;106;%4%1: General monitoring upper warning limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;107;%4%1: General monitoring upper warning limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;108;%4%1: General monitoring upper alarm limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;109;%4%1: General monitoring upper alarm limit exceeded.;User information;None
154;110;%4Paint pressure control for sensor %1 was activated by time program %2 but functionality is not enabled in cfg-editor;The painting pressure monitoring on min. or max. was activated in a time program, however, the monitoring function in the Cfg editor is not released for this sensor ;- Configure the painting pressure monitoring in the Cfg editor of 3DOnSite and release%CrLf%- Remove use of painting pressure monitoring for the named sensor in the time program 
154;111;%4%1: Resuming not possible because overpressure is still present.;The specified pressure sensor still reports an overpressure in the system. This overpressure must be relieved before application the can be continued;Switch in manual mode and then :%CrLf%- Start time program from group "Release overpressure" to relieve the pressure%CrLf%- Open the appropriate component (device) to relieve the pressure
154;112;%4Error overpressure at device %1: membrane valve opening pressure exceeded;During painting, the pressure at the indicated sensor is supervised. This exceeded the indicated limit. Defective valve/main needle, defecite dosing pump or blocked line may be causes for that.;If overpressure still present, release overpressure at first.  Optionally execute function check of valves. Exchange defective device. If a valve in the atomizer is affected, exchange atomizer.
154;113;%4Dosing pump in channel of pressure sensor %1 doesn't turn any more;The configured minimal painting pressure has not been reached during the complete painting process of the actual body to paint;- Verification of the dosing pump for paint flow -> drive clutch engaged or internally defective dosing pump.%CrLf%- For dosing pumps with pneumatic clutches, check pneumatic clutch activation at the valve terminal (MVS arm1)%CrLf%- Air in the paint system -> required pressures can not be achieved during test sequence -> drain paint to remove air%CrLf%- Pressure sensors defective -> replace pressure sensors%CrLf%- No paint supply ->ball valve closed, no pressure from the paint mixing room%CrLf%- Gearbox defective -> replace gearbox
154;114;%4Configuration error at supervision functionality paint pressure control minimum for pressure sensor %1;For the configured supervision, the configuration parameter 'CheckType' must be set on value =3 (absolut value);Check and correct configuration, then restart control.
155;101;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB MoveAbsolute error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;102;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB power error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;105;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB reset error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;106;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB ReadStatus error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;107;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB stop error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;108;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB ReadBackValues error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;109;%4Axis %1 error in the MFB ReadAxis error: %2 ;Project planning error in robot software.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;110;%4Encoder offset=%1 of drive %2 has changed. (Origin value %3). Restart robot controller !;Now parameters were loaded to the drive controller.;The new loaded parameters have overwritten the motor specific data.%CrLf%This specific data must be relaoded from the motor. Perform restart of the robort controller to reload the motor data.
155;111;%4New motor at %1 detected, Restart robot controller !;The serial number of the motor encoder has changed. Another motor was connected.%CrLf%The parameters from the motor name plate must be transmitted to drive controller.;Restart RPC-controller.
155;200;%4Piston %1, automatical mastering aborted, piston pressure > %2 bar ;During automatic piston mastering, the pressure in the piston has risen to more than the specified configured value. Possible causes: Valves that facilitate the drain of the medium in the piston have not been activated or do not switch ;Check time program "PistonMaster" and activate valves where appropriate. Check whether valves switch if activated manually
155;204;%4Piston %1, error while recreating drive parameter S92, actual value %2, weighting %3;After aborting the automatic piston referencing, the original value of the drive parameter S0-0092 could not be reconstructed. Either the currently read value was too small or the decimal places (weighting) of the value could not be determined;Determine original value of the parameter S0-0092 from data protection of the drive parameters for this drive and setting this value manually with the aid of DriveTop. 
155;205;%4Piston %1, drive parameter P51 = %2 out of range;The value of the drive parameter P51 is zero. Please check parameter ;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;206;%4Piston %1, drive parameter S111 = %2 out of range. Please check!;The value of the drive parameter S111 is zero. Please check parameter ;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;207;%4Piston %1, value S92 = %2 in drive is not consistent with the configured value = %3;Value of S92 in the drive does not agree with configured value (AxisMaxTorque) in process.cfg.%CrLf%Possible causes: %CrLf%- Autom. piston referencing aborted and original value of the S92 could not be written back into the drive.%CrLf%;- Check drive parameters, set S92 in the drive to original value where appropriate and master piston once again.%CrLf%- Adapt parameters in the process.cfg to value in the drive and master piston once again 
155;208;%4Piston %1, autom. mastering was aborted, because piston pressure at the start was higher than > %2 bar;When starting the referencing process, the pressure in the piston may be no higher than the specified configured value.;Relieve pressure in piston manually and restart referencing process 
155;209;%4Axis %1 error while reading parameter %2 from catalog;A parameter that is required by all means when initializing a process axis could not be found in the catalog of the control.;Check the current configuration of the control (Sercos part) and clarify why the required parameter is not contained.
155;210;%4Axis %1 parameter "posUnitsToIncrements invalid. value %2;For the correct calculation of the current torque of a process axis, two parameters must be available in the configuration of the control (Sercos part) with defined values.  %CrLf%- torqueUnitsToDriveValue = 10.0%CrLf%- driveType = ecodrive;Clarify why one or both parameters were entered into the configuration with different values.
155;213;%4Axis %1 not referenced.;Axis is not referenced.;Reference drive manually so that it can be displaced again.%CrLf%Then bring into its reference position and reference automatically/manually there.
155;214;%4Axis %1 error of drive control element. ;It was attempted to write a parameter to the respective drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
155;215;%4Axis %1 invalid speed required value %2, maximum %3 ;Speed required value is outside of the valid range;Check configuration and restart control.
155;216;%4Machine %1, axis %2 has reached the %3 software limit switch.;For the concerned axis, a target position was set outside of the traveling area.;Move corresponding axis into the permissible traveling range.
155;217;%4Machine %1, axis %2, target position beyond software end position %3. ;For the concerned axis, a target position was set outside of the traveling area.;Move corresponding axis into the permissible traveling range.
155;218;%4Axis %1 rotating speed deviation (required %2 rpm) - (actual %3 rpm) ;Speed required value is outside of the valid range;Set grinding-in speed to a regular value (V25 or V50).
155;219;%4No feedback speed OK from drive control element %1.;In the parameterized time, there was no feedback that the motor is working after the motor has been switched on.;Check and/or press motor overload switch.%CrLf% Check direction of rotation and change poles at the plug where appropriate.%CrLf%Phases and backup fuses.
155;220;%4No feedback voltage supply OK from drive control element %1.;In the external tension supply, an error has occurred.%CrLf%The consequence of this error is a disconnection of the regulator! ;Check supply voltage of the affected switch cabinet and eliminate fault where appropriate.
155;221;%4Axis %1, autom. mastering aborted since maximum limit (%2 mm) was crossed during the positioning ;- Carriage/skid position during start of automatic mastering not on master position %CrLf%- too high moment occurred %CrLf%- too long movement without encountering the obstacle to be expected (e.g. because not docked);- Push skid on correct master position %CrLf% check whether Cfg parameters have been set correctly %CrLf% check whether docking has occured correctly during the automatic mastering
155;222;%4Axis %1, measured torque %2 exceeds maximum %3;Error in movement ride while mastering automatically;- Push skid on correct master position %CrLf% check whether Cfg parameters have been set correctly %CrLf% check whether docking has occured correctly during the automatic mastering
155;223;%4Drive %1: Limit switch reached: %2.;The respective drive has activated the mechanical axis limit switch.;Verify reference position of axis. Check value of axis limit in controller configuration. Check value of axis limit in drive parameterization. 
155;224;%4Drive %1 has reached positive axis limit switch position %2;The respective drive has activated the mechanical axis limit switch.;Verify reference position of axis. Check value of axis limit in controller configuration. Check value of axis limit in drive parameterization. 
155;225;%4No access to input %1 of axis limit switch drive: %2. ;The mentioned hardware endpoint could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware end points in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input/output was not created or several inputs/outputs in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with circuit diagram, then restart control.
