181;100;%4%1: Error in the power stage;In the power stage of the Swirl regulator, an error has occurred.%CrLf%The consequence of this error is a disconnection of the regulator!;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;101;%4%1: Disturbance in external voltage supply;In the external tension supply, an error has occurred.%CrLf%The consequence of this error is a disconnection of the regulator! ;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;102;%4%1: Internal error in the Swirl controller;In the Swirl regulator, an internal error has occurred.%CrLf%The consequence of this error is a disconnection of the regulator!;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;103;%4%1: Error in logic module supply (24 V);In the supply of the logic module (24 V) an error has occurred.%CrLf%The consequence of this error is a disconnection of the regulator!  ;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;104;%4%1: All Swirl sensors are in status 0;All HALL sensors of the Swirl are in the status 0.%CrLf%- Wire breakage at sensor lines%CrLf%- Sensor no longer correct aligned %CrLf%- Internal error;Eliminate error.
181;105;%4%1: All Swirl sensors are in status 1;All HALL sensors of the Swirl are in the status 1.%CrLf%- Short circuit between sensor lines%CrLf%- Sensor no longer correct aligned %CrLf%- Internal error;Eliminate error.
181;106;%4%1: Faulty sequence of the Swirl sensors;The Swirl sensors were passed through in invalid sequence.;Check sensors, inlets and where appropriate counter cards and/or Swirl regulator, check parameterization.%CrLf%Remove fault.
181;107;%4%1: Short-circuit Swirl sensor %2;The Swirl regulator reports a short-circuit at the indicated sensor. Sensor or inlets faulty.%CrLf%Possibly wrong sense of rotation.;Check sensors, inlets and where appropriate counter cards and/or Swirl regulator, check parameterization.%CrLf%Remove fault.
181;108;%4%1: Cable breakdown Swirl sensor %2;The Swirl regulator reports a cable break at the indicated sensor. Sensor or inlets faulty.%CrLf%Possibly wrong sense of rotation.;Check sensors, inlets and where appropriate counter cards and/or Swirl regulator, check parameterization.%CrLf%Remove fault.
181;109;%4%1: General error Swirl controller;The swirl activation reported a general error.;Check sensors, inlets and where appropriate counter cards and/or Swirl regulator, check parameterization.%CrLf%Remove fault.
181;110;%4%1: Overcurrent cutoff Swirl controller triggered (reset at the device necessary);The overcurrent cut-off in the Swirl excitation was triggered.;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;111;%4%1: Monitoring of Swirl controller triggered (reset at the device necessary);The monitoring in the Swirl excitation was triggered (WatchDog).;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;112;%4%1: Voltage drop Swirl controller recognized (reset at the device necessary);A voltage drop was recognized in the Swirl excitation (BrownOut).;Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.%CrLf%Restart controller. Contact controller supplier in case of reappearance.
181;113;%4%1: Communication failure between Swirl controller and RPC controller;Communication failure due:%CrLf%- bus fault%CrLf%- fault of the optionally used gateway%CrLf%- fault of the Swirl controller;Check the bus connection and the possibly used gateway.%CrLf%Reset Swirl controller by means of RESET switch.%CrLf%Check electrics. Switch controller to idle.
182;1;%4%1: Subchannel %2 not found ;The specified subchannel was not found.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
182;2;%4%1: too many subchannels created (%2 - allowed: %3) ;Too many subchannels were created.%CrLf%Internal control problem.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
182;3;%4%1: Assigned channel cluster not found ;The assigned channel cluster was not found.%CrLf%Internal control problem;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
182;4;%4%1: No piston found in the related subchannel %2 ;The indicated hardware was not found in the related subchannel.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
182;5;%4%1: No pressure sensor found in the related subchannel %2 ;The indicated hardware was not found in the related subchannel.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
182;6;%4No exhaust valve has been assigned for the piston %1.;For the piston compensation, a discharge valve must be assigned to every piston. Error in the configuration.;Check configuration and restart control.
182;10;%4%1: No prepared channel available;During the application start or "flying piston splice" no prepared subchannel is available. Therefore, no (uninterruptible) application is possible.%CrLf%- Error or time-out during the preparation (filling, pressure setting)%CrLf%- Too high application volume.;Check current application volume%CrLf%- Check preparation 
182;12;%4%1: Piston change received from teach program, although manual piston change is deactivated;Piston change in the teach programm set, although the manual piston change is not released in the Process.cfg file.;Check parameterization in the 3DonSite process configuration (file process.cfg) and adjust where appropriate.%CrLf% Check teach program.
182;13;%4%1: Piston %2 was unselected, although this was currently being active.;Deselection of the indicated piston while this was in the painting status.;Acknowledge error and pay attention during the next deactivation that the piston is not the active piston.
182;15;%4%1: Wrong piston mode;Wrong control type for dosing piston. Control type must be between 0 and 5. ;Check brush table.
182;17;%4%1: Mode "MixedCirculation" not possible while application.;Wrong control type in brushtable.;Check brush table.
182;18;%4%1: Mode "MixedCirculation" not possible because wrong pressure sensor configured.;The parameter Checktype of the pressure monitoring is wrong.;The parameter Checktype of pressure monitoring must be 3.
182;19;%4%1: Mode "MixedCirculation" deactivated.;CFG-parameter EnableMixedCirculation is 0.;To use the control type "MixedCirculation" the parameter must be 1.
182;22;%4Main needle minimum switching time is smaller than / equal to the pre-warning time (actual: %1) ;The parameterized minimum response time is smaller than or equal to the prewarning time. As a minimum response time, the prewarning time is set.;Check parameterization in the 3DonSite process configuration and adjust where appropriate.
182;23;%4The maximum number (%1) of learnable painting volumes has been reached.;More painting volumes were used than were defined as learnable for the pre-pressure.;Check parameterization in the 3DOnSite process configuration (file Process.cfg) and adjust where appropriate.%CrLf%Turn off the learning where appropriate to delete the learned values and to restart the admission pressure learning. 
182;25;%4In the SetBrush order, the wrong main needle was indicated (BrushTrigger: %1, GunTrigger: %2);Error in the teaching program. -> Possible error during the learning of the pre-pressure;Check teach program and adapt.
182;26;%4The dosing piston was too long in pressure control mode.;The expected flow can't be reached without getting an overpressure.;Check material supply, check for leakage, check tempering system, check error time, check timeprogram
182;27;%4Pressure spike at main needle %1. Check seam.;Switch time of stated main needle changed.;Check switch time of stated main needle. Maybe time has to be changed in process configuration with 3DOnSite.
182;28;%4_ Pressure spike at main neelde %1. Check seam.;Switch time of stated main needle changed.;Check switch time of stated main needle. Maybe time has to be changed in process configuration with 3DOnSite.
185;1;%4%1: Error when reading parameter: %2 (group: %3) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;2;%4%1: Error when writing parameter: %2 (group: %3) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;3;%4%1: Error when reading the temperature actual values (group: %2) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;4;%4%1: Error when writing the temperature required values (group: %2) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;5;%4%1: Error when reading the percentage values (group: %2) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;6;%4%1: Error when investigating the current zone states (group: %2) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;7;%4%1: Error when activating the self optimization (group: %2) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;8;%4%1: Error when processing the global values (identification: %2) ;During the indicated write or reading access, an error has occurred.%CrLf%Faulty parameterization or transmission error.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;10;%4%1: Low alarm (zone: %2) ;If the value set as parameter 1 is undershot, the indicated zone reports Low alarm.%CrLf%The low alarm is not monitored with required value = 0!;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. %CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.
185;11;%4%1: High alarm (zone: %2) ;If the value set as parameter 2 is exceeded, the indicated zone reports High Alarm.%CrLf%The High Alarm is also monitored if required value = 0, to safely monitor short-circuited solid state relays at the output, also when zones are switched off;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. %CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.
185;12;%4%1: Heating current alarm (zone: %2) ;The heating current monitoring for the indicated zone was released. %CrLf%Either no current flow is recognized in case of excitation or a current flow is detected, although no excitation of the zone occurred.;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. Use device manual for error analysis.%CrLf%Repair fault and then acknowledge by means of: short power supply OFF/ON or changing and/or renewed setting of the required value of the faulty zone (activation/deactivation of the zone).
185;13;%4%1: Negative deviation alarm (zone: %2) ;As soon as the actual value of a zone differs by more than the value of the required value set as parameter 3, the indicated zone reports deviation alarm (negative = falling short, positive = transgression).;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. %CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.
185;14;%4%1: Positive deviation alarm (zone: %2) ;As soon as the actual value of a zone differs by more than the value of the required value set as parameter 3, the indicated zone reports deviation alarm (negative = falling short, positive = transgression).;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. %CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.
185;15;%4%1: Alarm due to required value change (zone: %2) ;The new required value of a zone differs by more than the value of the previously required value set as parameter 3.;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. %CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.
185;16;%4%1: Feeler break (zone: %2) ;The heating control element has detected a feeler break in the indicated zone.%CrLf%Heating or heating hose defective. Error in electric equipment. ;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. Use device manual for error analysis.%CrLf%Repair fault and then acknowledge by means of: short power supply OFF/ON or changing and/or renewed setting of the required value of the faulty zone (activation/deactivation of the zone).
185;17;%4%1: Feeler closure (zone: %2) ;The heating control element has detected a thermocouple closing in the indicated zone. Heating capacity is requested, but temperature does not rise.%CrLf%Wrongly connected or short-circuited cables. Heating or heating hose defective. Error in electrics.%CrLf%D;Check device status (LED's) and temperature. Use device manual for error analysis.%CrLf%Repair fault and then acknowledge by means of: short power supply OFF/ON or changing and/or renewed setting of the required value of the faulty zone (activation/deactivation of the zone).
185;18;%4%1: Error in optimization (zone: %2) ;During the internal self-optimization of the tempering device, an error occurred.;Check device status (LED's). use device manual for the error analysis.%CrLf%Check process parameter file and start indicated parameter correction where appropriate.%CrLf%Load process parameter file onto the control.%CrLf%Restart control. In case of repeated appearance, contact control supplier.
185;20;%4%1: Assigned temperature sensor %2 not found ;The temperature sensor indicated in the process parameter file was not found in the project.;Check parameterization and generate code new with ProcessBuilder, compile, restart control.
185;30;%4%1: Fuse dropped (zone: %2) ;The indicated fuse has failed.;Check fuse and turn back on
185;31;%4%1: FI circuit breaker dropped (zone: %2);The indicated fuse has failed.;Check fuse and turn back on
185;40;%4%1: Device hardware changed or not correctly detected - number of groups: %2 (%3);The device hardware is defective or was not correctly recognised during initialisation. The number of groups read out has an invalid value.;- If necessary, check the equipment hardware and/or replace.%CrLf%- Start reinitialisation (bus restart at sercos III).%CrLf%- Restart control system. If the error occurs again, contact control system supplier.
185;41;%4%1: Device hardware defective or not correctly detected - number of groups: %2;The device hardware is defective or was not correctly recognised during initialisation. The number of groups read out has an invalid value.;- If necessary, check the equipment hardware and/or replace.%CrLf%- Start reinitialisation (bus restart at sercos III).%CrLf%- Restart control system. If the error occurs again, contact control system supplier.
185;42;%4%1: The following zones are not assigned to a controlling device: %2 - run-up stopped;At least one zone in the software is not assigned to a controlling device. It is not possible to operate this (these) zone (s). The control system run-up has been stopped.;Export software with ProcessBuilder again and compile again.
185;43;%4%1: Zone number %2 allocated multiple times (%3) - operation not possible;The specified number is allocated to several zones. However, this zone number must be unambiguous and may only be assigned once per controlling device. The allocation to the hardware connections is made by means of this number.;Check parameterization in the 3DonSite process configuration and adjust where appropriate.
185;44;%4%1: Zone number %2 not supported by device hardware;The specified zone number is not supported by the device hardware (zone not available).;Check parameterization in the 3DonSite process configuration and adjust where appropriate.
186;1;%4%1: Invalid signal name '%2' while getting the signal address;It is attempted to determine with an invalid signal name a signal address.%CrLf%Controller is stopped due to this fatal error!;Check parameterization in the 3DOnSite process configuration (file Process.cfg) and restart controller. %CrLf%In case reappearance, generate code with ProcessBuilder again, compile and restart controller.%CrLf%Where appropriate, contact controller supplier.
186;10;%4%1: Rotation of masking device switched on, but after %2 still no feedback "mask rotating";The mask was turned on, but there is no feedback that the mask is turning.%CrLf%- Changed pneumatic settings%CrLf%- limit values for monitoring not correct%CrLf%- sensor for rotation monitoring defective%CrLf%- error air drive and/or;Check sensor for rotation monitoring.%CrLf% Check pneumatics (none or too small air supply for air drive). %CrLf% Check air drive and/or mask for sluggishness.%CrLf%Parameterization in the 3DOnSite process configuration (file Process.cfg).
186;11;%4%1: Upper warning limit for mask speed exceeded - required: %2;The indicated upper rotation speed limit for the mask was exceeded. %CrLf%- Changed pneumatic settings%CrLf%- limit values for monitoring not correct%CrLf%- sensor for rotation monitoring faulty%CrLf%- error air drive and/or free movement;Check sensor for rotation monitoring.%CrLf% Check pneumatics (too high air supply for air drive). %CrLf% Check air drive and/or mask for sluggishness.%CrLf% Check parameterization in the 3DOnSite process configuration (file Process.cfg).
