186;21;%4Valve %1 activated, but Ini %2 not occupied.;The indicated valve was activated and the indicated initiator was not occupied after the parameterized time.;Check the parameterization and the gauge / positioning device.
186;22;%4Valve %1 not activated, but Ini %2 occupied.;The indicated valve was not activated and the indicated initiator was not occupied in spite of that after a parameterized time.;Check the parameterization and the gauge / positioning device.
186;23;%4Initiator: %1 has the same state as initiator: %2.;The specified initiators have the same state.;Check control valves and specified initiators.
188;1;%4No feedback scrubber motor on. ;In the parameterized time, there was no feedback that the motor is working after the motor has been switched on.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
188;2;%4Device %1 on, but no feedback from %2.;The device was turned on, but there is no feedback -on-.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
188;3;%4No process release from safety PLC for the Sword Brush process;One of the process components (exhaust unit, cleaning brush or Ingromat valve) could not be turned on;The components listed are locked by the safety PLC. Please check the detailed error messages from the safety PLC
188;1001;%4Collision with scrubber at initiator %1.;The initiator announces a collision.;Check reason for the collision and eliminate.
188;1002;%4Collision with scrubber at initiator %1.;The initiator announces a collision.;Check reason for the collision and eliminate.
188;1003;%4No acknowledgement of flow guard that extraction is running.;No feedback that suction is running, B8;Check the flow guard, suction device or flexible suction tube
189;1;%4 Collision feather roller;The collision detection of the feather roller has tripped.%CrLf%- Collision between feather roller and car body%CrLf%- Collision detection is faulty.;Collision occured, retract roller in teach mode.%CrLf%No collision occured, check collision detection.
189;2;%4 No feedback form ionisation.;The ionisation was switched on, but no feedback from ionisation received.%CrLf%- Electrical connection faulty%CrLf%- Supply voltage not ok;- Check electrical connection%CrLf%- Check supply voltage
190;1;%4Roller %1: collision ;The collision detection has reacted ;Relieve roller. If no collision should have occurred, check the rope or the light barrier.
190;2;%4Roller %1: no valid profile data for type %2 at program start ;For the mentioned motor vehicle type, no profile data could be loaded.;For mentioned type, check profile with 3DOnSite and restore, observe error reports where appropriate
190;3;%4Roller %1: no reachable point or previous point found in profile type: %2 point: %3. ;No accessible point lying ahead (conveyor value > as current conveyor value) could be found in profile.%CrLf%Presumably error in the parameterization of the profile or conveyor has exceeded maximum profile position.;For mentioned type, check profile with 3DOnSite and restore, observe error reports where appropriate
190;4;%4Roller %1: no valid points found in profile type: %2.;The mentioned profile includes Invalid data.%CrLf%Presumably error in the parameterization of the profile or invalid file.;For mentioned type, check profile with 3DOnSite and restore, observe error reports where appropriate
190;5;%4Roller %1: no car body data available for the calculation of the points. ;Internal control problem or operating error.%CrLf%While movement program was running, the car body data were deleted, presumably by executing the "ClearFifo" command.;In the vision system, check the Fifo overview whether car body to be worked on is still available in the Fifo memory.%CrLf%Unselect machine and convey car body out.
190;6;%4Roller %1: No profile data for the calculation of the points of type: %2 available;For the mentioned motor vehicle type, no profile data could be loaded.;For mentioned type, check profile with 3DOnSite and restore, observe error reports where appropriate
190;8;%4Roller %1: Light barrier for collision detection soiled. ;The collision light barrier announces that it is dirty.;Clean light barrier and acknowledge warning message.
190;9;%4Roller %1: During the controller start, not all axes could be accessed. ;Internal control problem, programming error or parameterizing error.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
190;10;%4The selected reference position of machine %1 exceeds the softend. ;The reference position entered in the vision system lies beyond the end of the axis, would thus not be approachable.;Check entered reference position and correct.%CrLf%Carry out function once again.
190;13;%4- %1 Collision signal still active and safe position reached, check sensor. ;Due to a collision, the roller went into a safe position, the collision detection still announces an error, however. Presumably the collision detection was damaged or is faulty.;The collision detection must be checked.
190;15;%4Machine %1 axis %2: error when initializing the profile data for axis calculation. ;It was attempted to carry out an invalid operation. Control error, bug, error by debugging.;Acknowledge and restart. If the error is repeated, abort the car body and order again.
190;16;%4Machine %1 axis %2: error when initializing the acceleration for axis calculation. ;Internal control problem, programming error or parameterizing error.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
190;17;%4Machine %1 axis %2: error when calculating the path. ;During the path calculation, an internal control problem occurred. Called function "KCtrl" caused an error.;Acknowledge and restart. If the error is repeated, abort the car body and order again.
190;18;%4Drag error %1mm of axis %2 at conveyor position %3mm. ;Current axis position deviates more than configured value from the required position.;Reduce the speed of the concerned axis by changing the movement profile.
190;19;%4Roller %1: Could not load fixed position %2 programmnumber %3.;The mentioned profile includes Invalid data.%CrLf%Presumably error in the parameterization of the profile or invalid file.;For mentioned type, check profile with 3DOnSite and restore, observe error reports where appropriate
190;20;%4Mastering was started by HMI for an nonexistent axis. Machine %1, Axis %2.;Configuration of HMI does not fit to the configuration of the RPC.;Adjust configuration of HMI with the configuration of the RPC.
190;21;%4Moved to save position because of collision of %1 but position lies out of profile free area.;Save position is not in profile free area.;- Move to save position in mode manual and check at visualisation if profile free switch is signaled. %CrLf%- Reteach save psoition with 3D-OnSite is necesary.
190;22;%4Roller %1: collision ;The collision detection has reacted ;Relieve roller. If no collision should have occurred, check the rope or the light barrier.
190;23;%4Machine %1, Profile %2, Point %3 Full correction of the roller diameter isn't possible (Setvalue>Max).;Due to correction of the roller diameter the resulting set value of an axis in mentioned point is out axis limit. Because of that a full correction of the roller diameter isn't possible.;Reduction of the correction value for roller diameter in the configuration of the machine.
191;1;%4Timeout when loading the profile files for type %1. ;No profile data could be loaded for mentioned type.%CrLf% - Pitch in ghost mode too small.%CrLf%- Faulty profile file.;Check pitch%CrLf%Check profile file with 3DOnSite and save again.
192;7;%4Timeout for feedback of air supply. ;After the air supply was turned on, no pressure was built up.;Check air supply.
192;9;%4- %1 Timeout for feedback of the ionization. ;After the switch-on of the ionization, no feedback occurred.;Check ionization%CrLf%Check supply voltage of the ionization.
193;6;%4The initiator %1 does not report any movement although the pump is activated.;-Pump coupling defective %CrLf%- Initiator defective %CrLf%- cable connection interrupted;- Check pump coupling %CrLf%- Check initiator %CrLf% Check cable connections
193;8;%4Device %1: The parameter "%2" has an invalid value (%3).;Parameter outside of the permissible area;Correct Cfg parameter
193;101;%4device %1: Leakage monitoring is deactivated;Leakage monitoring is deactivated;Activate leakage monitoring in PCUx.cfg
193;102;%4device %1: Leakage occurred;Leakage occurred;Eliminate leak and acknowledge error.
193;103;%4device %1: Leakage occurred;Leakage occurred;Eliminate leak and acknowledge error.
194;1;The proximity switches report more than one position.;- proximity switch in Cleaner B is triggered by mistake or is defect%CrLf%- cable break%CrLf%- faulty process configuration (parameter "InverseInitators");Check for possible cable break and verify the correct behavior of initiators
196;1;%4Invalid state for device %1 (set=%2);ColorStopValve have only state 0(closed), 1(auto) and 2(open);Check the communication to the HMI.
196;2;%4Invalid set values for device %1 in time program %2. Only one set value possible (auto or open);Device got set values for state auto and open at the same time. This is not possible.;Check the parameterization in time program.
197;1;%4Incorrect switching status for device %1 from the HMI interface.;Inadmissible switching condition from HMI interface. Allowed are 0 (= no required value from HMI), 1 (=dock), 2 (=undock), 3 (=reset required values);Check the communication to the HMI.
197;2;%4Incorrect parameterisation of device %1 in Time program %2. Only one switching status possible (Set_R, Set_V or Reset);The device receives more than one drive signal simultaneously (R (=dock), V (=undock), reset (=do not activate). This is not permissible.;Check the parameterization in time program.
199;1;%4The nozzle changer does not contain any valid data.;The administration data of the nozzle changer are invalid.;Enter data for nozzle changer in vision system.
199;2;%4The nozzle information of HN%1 could not be transmitted to the change place no. %2.;The initiator of the nozzle change place is not assibned in spite of extended bolt.;Check initiator and nozzle change head. Correct data for the nozzle changer in vision system where appropriate.
199;3;%4The bolt at the change place no. %1 was extended and/or retracted with a wrong main needle HN number (%2).;In the teach program, an invalid main needle number was set.;Check teach program and correct data for the nozzle changer in vision system where appropriate.
199;4;%4The initiator at the change place %1 has changed from occupied to not occupied with extended bolt.;Defective initiator or defective cabling at the indicated nozzle change place.;Check initiator and cabling and exchange where appropriate.
199;5;%4The status of a nozzle in the exchange place can only be changed with extended bolt.;An attempt was made to change the status of the nozzle manually to OK. When this was done, the nozzle was not fixed.;Extend bolt of nozzle exchange place and then change the nozzle status to ok.
199;6;%4There is a nozzle at changer place %1 which is not OK. The type is %2 and there are %3 OK nozzles of this type in the changer;The robot has deposited a not ok nozzle of the specified type in the nozzle changer.;Replace nozzle on next occasion.
200;3;%4SCU - SAFETY: personnel protection is jumpered (light barrier);User information;None
200;5;%4SCU - SAFETY: timeout safety monitoring time "T2 without action";The dead man switch at the teach pendant was not activated for a longer time. Therefore, the safety release was withdrawn.;Acknowledge fault  Reselect T2 mode.
200;6;%4SCU - SAFETY: process technology is jumpered (ventilation) ;User information;None
200;7;%4SCU - SAFETY: timeout jumpering process technology (ventilation) ;Key-operated switch for the bridging of the process engineering was activated too long.;Activate key switch once again, acknowledge error where appropriate.
200;8;%4SCU - SAFETY: general emergency stop error ;An emergency off switch in the zone was activated.;- Verify why emergency off was released. %CrLf%- If there is no danger, bring emergency off button into OK position, acknowledge error.
200;9;%4SCU - SAFETY: error ventilation / process technology;Ventilation and/or washout were switched off. Therefore, the installation was transferred into a safe operating state.;The error can be acknowledged if the external alarm does not exist anymore.
200;10;%4SCU - SAFETY: fire alarm ;The fire alarm station announces a fire alarm. Therefore, the installation was transferred into a safe operating state.;The error can be acknowledged if the external alarm does not exist anymore.
200;11;%4SCU - SAFETY: no general release 'safety ok' from safety-plc;The safety PLC has detected a safety-relevant error and therefore revoked the overall release.;Read detailed fault messages. Acknowledge fault.
200;14;%4SCU - SAFETY: conveyor jumpered on panel - please unselect all robots and switch control-voltage off ;User information;None
200;15;%4SCU - SAFETY: error ventilation / booth process technology (direct signal);Ventilation and/or washout were switched off. Therefore, the installation was transferred into a safe operating state.;The error can be acknowledged if the external alarm does not exist anymore.
200;16;%4SCU - SAFETY: emergency stop - desk;An emergency off switch in the zone was activated.;- Verify why emergency off was released. %CrLf%- If there is no danger, bring emergency off button into OK position, acknowledge error.
200;17;%4SCU - SAFETY: emergency stop - teach-pendant / switch-box 1;An emergency off switch in the zone was activated.;- Verify why emergency off was released. %CrLf%- If there is no danger, bring emergency off button into OK position, acknowledge error.
200;18;%4SCU - SAFETY: Emergency Stop - external;An emergency off switch in the zone was activated.;- Verify why emergency off was released. %CrLf%- If there is no danger, bring emergency off button into OK position, acknowledge error.
200;20;%4SCU - SAFETY: error personnel-protection;Unauthorized entering of the safety zone.;Check whether any persons are inside the safe region. Acknowledge error.
200;52;%4SCU - datacheck ini set - but no dataset found in inlet fifo  ;There are no data for the object on the data check initiator.;Enter data manually in reselection mask.
200;53;%4SCU - object could not be added to inlet fifo because it was already full;The fixing of the car body was removed during the processing. The installation was stopped then immediately.;Fix car body again, then acknowledge error and continue processing. Attention: increased danger of collision.%CrLf%Alternatively, bring the robots into home position (e.g. in T1) and then convey the car body out.
200;55;%4SCU - data record could not be added to feed fifo, because this was already full;It was attempted to write a new car body data record into an already full input buffer;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
200;56;%4SCU - conveyor is running without conveyor release. WARNING: DANGER OF COLLISION! ;The conveyor is running without conveyor release. Possibly there is a programming error in the conveyor equipment control or the conveyor equipment is in manual mode.;Stop station and deselect robot to prevent that robots are started and collisions happen this way.
200;57;%4SCU - No message "conveyor ready" from conveyor equipment;Conveyor is not ready to start.;None
200;60;%4SCU - object fixed in zone, but no data in fifo. Please insert data manually;User information;None
200;61;%4SCU - conveyor-inlet is locked;User information;None
200;62;%4SCU - conveyor is not enabled (operator panel);User information;None
200;100;%4SCU - timeout during reselection;During the reselection, a time-out occurred. Possible causes: %CrLf%- Programming error in PLC%CrLf%- No acknowledgement of at least one robot controller.;Check Fifo data in PLC and all robot controllers.%CrLf%Where appropriate delete all data (ClearFifo).
200;101;%4SCU - at least one dataset in fifo is invalid ;There is at least one invalid data record in the data fifos. Possible cause: %CrLf%- Data record not entered into type or paint assignment table;Find faulty data record by means of reselection window and reselect (e.g. to valid type or color and/or to "do not apply").
200;102;%4SCU - RESELECTION: operation in ghost inlet fifo not allowed;User information;None
200;103;%4SCU - reselection already active/still running ;User information;None
200;104;%4SCU - RESELECTION: no dataset selected ;User information;None
200;105;%4SCU - reselection: 'change selection' could not be carried out;User information;None
200;150;%4SCU - high tension not activated (operator panel) ;Station cannot be started, because the high tension was not activated on the control panel (key-operated switch);Connect high tension on the control panel or deselect high tension of all robots.
200;151;%4SCU - type page not found in assignment table ;Type data could not be found in type assignment table.;Check type assignment table. Enter missing type where appropriate. After that, correct data by reselection.
200;152;%4SCU - color page not found in assignment table ;Paint data could not be found in paint assignment table.;Check paint assignment table. Enter missing paint/color where appropriate. After that, correct data by reselection.
200;153;%4SCU - operation not allowed - lock conveyor inlet first (robot in flowcheck) ;User information;Block zone inlet.
200;154;%4SCU - operation not allowed - inlet conveyor may not be unlocked (robot in flowcheck) ;User information;Before unlocking the zone inlet, bring the robots into the home position.
200;155;%4SCU - burner not activated (operator panel) ;Station cannot be started, because the burner was not activated on the control panel (key-operated switch);Connect burner on the control panel or deselect burner of all robots.
200;156;%4SCU - external color not found - color code in color assignment table not found on interface to external paint supply ;The special paint supply currently does not provide the desired paint color. Therefore, the data record could not completely be generated.;Wait until special color supply provides the color, then correct data record by reselection.%CrLf%OR: reselect data record to " Do not apply".
200;157;%4SCU - negative conveyor movement detected - fifo data were reset ;User information;None
200;158;%4SCU - CLEAR FIFO - fifo data was deleted ;User information;None
200;159;%4SCU - station can not be started - enable power of motion-drives first;User information;None
200;160;%4SCU - station can not be started - enable power of process-drives first;User information;None
200;200;%4SCU - cannot start ghost - body in zone ;The ghost mode must not be started as long as there is a real car body in the zone (collision danger).;Convey car body out of zone. If it should a faulty state (no car body in the zone) delete the data (ClearFifo).
200;201;%4SCU - no ghost start allowed - inlet conveyor not locked;User information;Block zone inlet.
200;202;%4SCU - GHOST: station not in automatic or no station start ;Start of the ghost mode is only possible if: %CrLf%- station is in automatic%CrLf%- station started;Start station in "Automatic" mode.
200;203;%4SCU - GHOST: no ghost selected ;For the start of the ghost mode,> at least one ghost data record must be selected.;Select at least one ghost data record.
200;204;%4SCU GHOST: invalid body gap, possibly too small ;User information;Check set ghost pitch and correct where appropriate.
200;205;%4SCU - ghost mode active. Zone entrance may not be unlocked .;The zone inlet must not be released as long as the ghost mode is active (collision danger).;End ghost mode, then clear zone inlet.
200;206;%4SCU - ghost mode was stopped because of incoming real object - CLEAR ALL FIFOS - INCONSISTENT DATA! ;During the ghost mode, a real object was booked into the zone. This is not permissible. Possible causes: %CrLf%- Programming error in the PLC%CrLf%- programming error in the conveyor equipment control%CrLf%- Manual intervention in the conveyor equipment.;This is a not permissible special case. Therefore, the zone data must be deleted (ClearFifo).
200;207;%4SCU - ghost without movement only in position 'flow check' allowed;User information;Bring robot into the flow check position, then start ghost mode.
200;208;%4SCU - unselect all handling robots for 'ghost without movement' ;User information;Deselect all handling robots, then start ghost mode.
200;210;%4SCU - gap ghost cannot be started, gap ghost already active ;User information;None
200;213;%4SCU - GHOST: not all robots are in position home;User information;None
200;250;%4SCU - FIXPOS: station not in mode hand ;The approaching of fixed positions is only permissible in manual mode.;Change over to manual mode.
200;251;%4SCU - FIXPOS: no robot selected ;User information;Select a robot on the fixed position mask.
200;252;%4SCU - FIXPOS: no target position selected;User information;Select a target position on the fixed position mask.
200;253;%4SCU - FIXPOS: collision interlock - forbidden fixpos request from HMI;The desired fixed position ride is currently not possible (collision danger).;Check position of other robots. Where appropriate, further error message give information about the precise locking reason.
200;254;%4SCU - FIXPOS: collision interlock door opener not in home position ;Fixed position ride not permissible, because the door openers are not in home position (collision danger).;First, bring door opener into home position.
200;255;%4SCU - FIXPOS: collision interlock - object in zone ;Fixed position ride not permissible, since there is a car body in the station (collision danger).;Convey car body out of zone. If it should a faulty state (no car body in the zone) delete the data (ClearFifo).
200;256;%4SCU - FIXPOS: fixposition interlock of PLC jumpered by user via vision system;User information;None
200;300;%4SCU - communication-error to conveyor-control;Miswiring or hardware defect. %CrLf%Communication fault or bus failure.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
200;350;%4SCU - STATISTIC: timeout transfering statistic-data to server;User information;None
200;351;%4SCU - STATISTIC: overflow of statistic-sending-buffer - statistic-dataset lost;- No network link%CrLf%- Vision system not started%CrLf%- robot controller not working;- Check network link%CrLf%- Restart vision system%CrLf%- Restart robot controller
200;352;%4SCU - LINE-STATISTIC: timeout transfering statistic-data to server;User information;None
200;353;%4SCU - LINE-STATISTIC: overflow of statistic-sending-buffer - statistic-dataset lost;- No network link%CrLf%- Vision system not started%CrLf%- robot controller not working;- Check network link%CrLf%- Restart vision system%CrLf%- Restart robot controller
200;400;%4SCU - external conveyor-stop;User information;None
201;1;%4SCU - %1 no heartbeat from RPC ;- The communication to the robot is faulty (field bus)%CrLf%- The robot controller is stopped.;Check whether robot controller is operating (vision system, teach pendant or remote desktop)%CrLf%Where appropriate, check field bus.
201;2;%4SCU - %1 bad acknowledge of transferred body data-set;The robot controller has acknowledged the transferred data as "invalid".;Evaluate detailed error information from the robot. Correct data by reselection where appropriate.
201;3;%4SCU - %1 bad acknowledge of transferred vision displacement data;The robot controller has acknowledged the transferred camera displacing values as "invalid".;Start measurement manually. Check camera system.
201;4;%4SCU - %1 brake check failed;User information;Check brake
201;5;%4SCU - %1 timeout changeover drives to AB;While the robot drives were connected, a time-out occurred.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
201;6;%4SCU - %1 timeout changeover process to AB;While the robot drives were connected, a time-out occurred.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
201;7;%4SCU - %1 position bypass forced on HMI ;User information;None
201;8;%4SCU - %1 high tension selected on vision system, but no safety release;The high tension cannot be connected since the safety release is missing.;Read detailed fault messages. Acknowledge fault.
201;9;%4SCU - %1 Multi-K: pot time warning;User information;None
201;10;%4SCU - %1 Multi-K: pot time alarm ;The maximum service life of the material is reached, the robot must be purged urgently.;Bring installation into the manual or automatic mode and connect drives in such a way that emergency purging can be carried out.
201;11;%4SCU - %1 unselection only in position unselect possible;The user has tried to unselect the robot outside of the deactivation area. This is not permissible, since otherwise there will be collision danger with the conveyor / other robots.;Bring robot into the deselection area.
201;12;%4SCU - %1 no conveyor release from robot;The conveyor was stopped due to the missing conveyor release of the robot.;Read detailed fault messages. Acknowledge fault.
201;13;%4SCU - %1 paint relevant collective error;The robot controller has found an error which makes a continuation of the application impossible.;Read detailed fault messages. Acknowledge fault.
201;14;%4SCU - %1 collective error;User information;None
201;15;%4SCU - %1 emergency stop from TP;An emergency off switch in the zone was activated.;- Verify why emergency off was released. %CrLf%- If there is no danger, bring emergency off button into OK position, acknowledge error.
201;16;%4SCU - %1 error stop station from robot;The robot station has stopped all robots of the station due to an internal error (error class "StopStation").;Read detailed fault messages. Acknowledge fault.
201;17;%4SCU - %1 robot may not be selected because it is disabled  ;The user has tried to select the robot. This is currently not possible, however, because the robot was deactivated: %CrLf%- emergency mode active%CrLf%- robot controller turned off %CrLf%- robot in maintenance box%CrLf%...;Cancel deactivation, then select robot again.
201;18;%4SCU - %1 robot may not be selected while program is running ;The selecting of the robot is not permissible since the other robots already have an active program.;Wait until the other robots have finished the processing. Then select robot.
201;19;%4SCU - %1 fixpositioning not possible - drives have no power;The robot cannot carry out any fixed position ride, because the drives currently do not have any power.;Check whether power has been connected. Read detailed fault messages. Check drive for errors. Contact control supplier where appropriate.
201;20;%4SCU - %1 fixpositioning not possible - robot not selected on HMI ;The robot cannot carry out the desired fixed position ride, because this is selected /deselected.;Select robot.
201;21;%4SCU - %1 fixpositioning not possible - robot fixpos sequence already/still active ;The user has attempted to start a new fixed position ride while another one was still being active.;Acknowledge error and wait until active fixed position ride is finished. Abort fixed position ride where appropriate.
201;22;%4SCU - %1 station cannot be started - robot not in home position;The station start is only possible if all robots are in home position.;Bring robot into home position.
201;23;%4SCU - %1 error ex-controller ;The purging controller of the robot announces an error. Possible causes: %CrLf%- Loss of air supply%CrLf%- leakage at the robot / housing not closed%CrLf%- purging process active after power failure;The purging may take up to 5 minutes. If the error cannot be acknowledged then, check the air supply or the tightness of the robot housing.
201;24;%4SCU - %1 timeout - no 'acknowledge start tracking' from robot;Missing acknowledgement of the conveyor equipment signal from robot. Internal error.;Check file content of all robots for plausibility, delete data where appropriate (ClearFifo). %CrLf% Contact control supplier.
201;25;%4SCU - %1 timeout - no 'acknowledge body incoming' from robot;Missing acknowledgement of the conveyor equipment signal from robot. Internal error.;Check file content of all robots for plausibility, delete data where appropriate (ClearFifo). %CrLf% Contact control supplier.
201;26;%4SCU - %1 timeout - no 'acknowledge body in position' from robot;Missing acknowledgement of the conveyor equipment signal from robot. Internal error.;Check file content of all robots for plausibility, delete data where appropriate (ClearFifo). %CrLf% Contact control supplier.
201;27;%4SCU - %1 timeout - no 'acknowledge part-detect' from robot;Missing acknowledgement of the conveyor equipment signal from robot. Internal error.;Check file content of all robots for plausibility, delete data where appropriate (ClearFifo). %CrLf% Contact control supplier.
201;28;%4SCU - %1 timeout feedback signal solvent safety valve of bell cleaner;The feedback of the pressure switch for the solvent valve of the atomizer cleaning device is unplausible. Therefore either the%CrLf%- high tension cannot be turned on%CrLf%- or the atomizer cleaning cannot be carried out.;Check feedback of the pressure switch in safety PLC.
201;29;%4SCU - %1 robot is disabled - degrade mode active ;User information;None
201;30;%4SCU - %1 no movement release in teach mode - robot is unselected ;The user has tried to connect the drives of the robot in the teach mode (dead man switch) while the robot is being unselected.;Select robot in vision system
201;31;%4SCU - %1 re-initialization of robot is active ;User information;None
201;32;%4SCU - %1 RPC data feedback: object id not found in PLC fifo ;The statistical data reported back from the robot controller could not be related - BodyID unknown. Possibly the object had already been deleted from the memory of the PLC.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
201;33;%4SCU - %1 timeout while transferring data to Rpc (FB_RpcInit) ;During the handover of the data to the robot controller, a time-out occurred.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
201;34;%4SCU - %1 plausibility check of robot modes failed - RPC does not acknowledge selected operating mode ;The required operating mode of the robot controller does not agree with the actual operating mode - internal error.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
201;35;%4SCU - %1 robot in teach mode T1/T2 ;User information;None
201;36;%4SCU - no conveyor inlet release from robot - material heater not ready;Wait until the material has the right temperature. The inlet will be unblocked automatically. Check filling level of water quench. Unselect process of robot to continue without application.;Wait until the material has the right temperature. The inlet will be unblocked automatically. Check filling level of water quench. Unselect process of robot to continue without application.%CrLf%
201;37;%4SCU - %1 High voltage is locked after atomizer-cleaning - move robot to home-position;For safety reasons the high voltage is blocked after a atomizer cleaning until the robot is back in home position. Currently the robot does not send a request for atomizer cleaning but is also not in home position. So the high voltage is still blocked and can not be enabled. Possible causes:%CrLf%- Error in the sequence or time program%CrLf%- time program was aborted (e.g. deselection, RPC restart)%CrLf%- programming fault;Move robot to home position. This can be done either with a fixposition command on HMI or via TP in T1. Attention: Danger of collisions!
201;38;%4SCU - %1 High voltage is locked after handling - move robot to home-position;For safety reasons the high voltage for paint robots with additional handling tool is blocked during handling. Blocking and unblocking is done in the teach program.%CrLf%At the moment the high voltage is blocked, but the robot has no active teach program. This is an error state. Possible reasons:%CrLf%- Teach program was aborted e.g. by robot unselection%CrLf%- robot controller was re-booted%CrLf%- error in teach program.;Move robot to home position. This can be done either with a fixposition command on HMI or via TP in T1. Attention: Danger of collisions!%CrLf%Background information:%CrLf%After an abort of the program it must be ensured, that the handler is no longer near the car body. Because of this the robot must be moved to home position once.
201;39;%4SCU - %1 Monitoring area around atomizer cleaning device: High voltage is active / not unloaded.;The area around the atomizer cleaning device is monitored. In this area the high voltage may not be active. Possible causes:%CrLf%- The atomizer entered this area although the high voltage was not unloaded. To prevent an ignition the robot was stopped.%CrLf%- The high voltage was enabled, while the atomizer was in the monitoring area.;Do not enable high voltage while the atomizer is near the atomizer cleaning device.%CrLf%Check teach program and orientation of the atomizer. Keep distance to the atomizer cleaning device.%CrLf%Check if the point 'InBox' is correctly teached.%CrLf%With active time program: Check if the property 'high voltage safe off' is correctly configured.%CrLf%Unselect high voltage.%CrLf%Contact the supplier.
201;40;%4SCU - %1 Monitoring area around atomizer cleaning device: Plausibility fault with 'InBox' signal.;A cleaning cycle was started. During the complete cycle the signal 'atomizer in atomizer cleaning device' (InBox) was not detected a single time.;Check if the point 'InBox' is correctly teached.%CrLf%Unselect high voltage.%CrLf%Contact the supplier.
220;1;%4 SCP: Ex-Controller has switched off;Ex-controller alarm is activ. Robot is leaky or purging is activ.;- Robot is leaky: Check if all service apertures and ports are closed leaktight.%CrLf%- Check air supply of Ex-controller%CrLf%- Ex-controller purging is activ: Wait until purging is completed.
220;2;%4SCP: Brake release device pluged;Brake release device is connected.;Disconnect the brake release device and put on the blind plug
220;3;%4SCP: Feedback error 24V supply;Feedback error of 24 V contactors;Check contactor and feedback line
220;4;%4SCP: Error feedback line of load contactor;Error feedback line of load contactor;Feedback Error of Load contactor. Check contactor and feedback line.
220;5;%4SCP: Error feedback line of high tension contactor;Feedback error of high tension contactor;Check contactor and feedback line.
220;6;%4SCP: Error feedback line of air heater contactor. ;Error in feedback line of air heater contactor;Check contactor and feedback line.
220;7;%4No heartbeat from SCP;No comunication of controller;Restart controller (Switch off and on )
220;8;%4SCP: No Heartbeat from PLC;No comunication of controller;Check profisafe kommunication from PLC to SCP
220;9;%4The robot has exceeded the velocity %1;Configuration in Robotcontrol and SCP are different;Check configuration and set the correct values.
220;10;%4The robot has exceeded the permissible velocity %1;Configuration in Robotcontrol and SCP are different;Check configuration and set the correct values.
220;11;%4One of the main axes has exceeded the permissible velocity;Configuration in Robotcontrol and SCP are different;Check configuration and set the correct values.
220;12;%4No reference of the robot drives for the safety control - Execute referencing.;The safety control needs the reference of the robot drives to verify their position. This reference is existing.;Move robot in T1-mode to Fixpos RefPos and execute referencing by teach pendant or EcoScreen.
220;13;%4Mode automatic is not allowed as long as the safety control is not synchronized.;Is the safety control not sychronized the robot isn't allowed to move fast than 250mm/sec.%CrLf%This would lead to a bad application result.%CrLf%Because of that the automatic mode is not allowed in this situation.;Switch station to mode "Hand" and move the robot to fixed position SYNC by EcoScreen.%CrLf%When the robot has reached the position and the signal form the initiator is received, the sychronisation is executed.
220;14;%4Robot position not synchronized with safety control - Execute synchronisation.;The axis positions have to be synchronized with the safety control to ensure the correct surveillance of the robot.;Move robot to the fixpoition SyncPos. If initiator is switching in this position the verification of the axis position is done.
220;15;%4Robot has left the safe working area.;The configuration of the safety controller doesn't match with the configuration of the robot.;Verfiy the configration of the safety controller with configuration of the robot.
220;100;%4Testpuls error  %1 at an SDI input;Wrong TDO input;Check wiring and configuration of the digital input 
220;101;%4Loss-of-Load error %1 output SBC;Current at output is less than 80 mA;Check output connection, load must be more than 80 mA
220;102;%4Plausibility error %1 axis %2;The difference between the safety signals is more than configuert.;- Check configuration%CrLf%- Check wiring of feedback plug
220;103;%4 Deviation rawposition encoder %1 axis %2;- Encoder rawposition between System A and System B different;- Restart device. %CrLf%- Check encoder%CrLf%- Change motor
220;104;%4Wrong encoder type connected axis %2;Configured and connected encodertype not equal;- Ccheck connected Motor (Motortyp?)%CrLf%- Check plug (pins)%CrLf%- Check configuration
220;105;%4 Faulty switching of output SBCx. %2;- Short circuit of output with 24 V or 0 V%CrLf%- Brake release device is in use;- Check output wiring (short-cut, cross circuit)%CrLf%- Disconnect the brake release device and reconnect the terminal plug%CrLf%- Quitt error and / or power reset
220;106;%4 Faulty switching of output (dynamic test) for SBCx.0 to SBCx.5;- Short circuit of output with 24 V or 0 V%CrLf%- Brake release device is in use;- Check output wiring (short-cut, cross circuit)%CrLf%- Disconnect the brake release device and reconnect the terminal plug%CrLf%- Quitt error and / or power reset
220;107;%4 Faulty internal power supply of the encoderbox ( %1 );Supply voltage of the module not correct or component fault on the module;Check device supply voltage and switch device off / on
220;108;%4 Timeout during writing of the encoder index RCU%1;Error by writing the encoder index;Switch of and on the system. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
234;1001;%4Invalid process-order from EcoTalk.;-Invalid entry in file: EcotalkVariables.ttp%CrLf%-Error in EcoTalk program;* Correct the EcoTalk program%CrLf%* Correct the EcotalkVariables.ttp file.
234;1002;%4New process-order "%1" from EcoTalk before the command "%2" was finished.;Error in the EcoTalk program: A new process command was transmitted before the preceding command was processed.;A SET_??? must always be ended with a RECEIVE_??? first, before a new command may be set to the process with SET_???. Here, the chronological processing (MainRun, PreRun, stop) of the command must be observed.
234;1003;%4Command %1 cannot be carried out, because since device %2 is not available;A device required for the execution of the command from EcoTalk is not available in the process configuration.;- Remove the EcoTalk command in the teach program that is not executable. %CrLf%- Add the missing device in the process configuration
234;3001;%4Process-order %1 acknowledged without action, because the atomizer was deselected.;User information;None
234;3002;%4RunTimeprogram from EcoTalk not possible, because Hightension is not switched off.;The EcoTalk command for the shutdown of the high tension was not carried out correctly.;Check whether the command for the shutdown of the high tension is called in the EcoTalk program before the time program is carried out.
234;3003;%4The command will not be carried out, because Pushout is already started.;User information;None
240;2;%4Timeout in the degradation of the high voltage for handling (HighTension device);No feedback from high tension device  that high voltage is off%CrLf%Maybe the actual value of the high voltage is still too large;Check if actual value is really too high (e.g by using the HMI)%CrLf%Determine and correct the cause of excessive voltage / no correct discharge
