365;4;%4Fuse 24V supply UPS dropped;Fuse 6F4, 6F5, 6F7 or 6F8 de-energized;Check fuse and turn back on
365;5;%4UPS power supply not ok;Circuit breaker 6Q1 de-energized;Check fuse and turn back on
365;6;%4UPS not ready to operate;Circuit breaker 6Q1 de-energized;Check fuse and turn back on
365;7;%4Protective motor control 400V dropped ;Circuit breaker 24Q4 or 60Q2 de-energized;Check fuse and turn back on
365;12;%4Fuse 24V supply process dropped. ;Fuse 7F3 or 7F4 de-energized;Check fuse and turn back on
365;13;%4Motor holding brake is opened ;The motor blocking brake was opened externally.%CrLf%With opened brake, it not is possible to connect the drives.;Close motor blocking brake.
365;18;%4Fuse one-phase supply for external panels dropped.;User information;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
365;24;%4The set maximum temperature in the switch cabinet %1 was exceeded;The preset maximum temperature at 4S1 /4S4 is exceeded.%CrLf%Cooling defective or temperature set too low;Check temperature settings. Check air conditioning unit.
365;25;%4The set maximum temperature in the switch cabinet %1 was exceeded;The preset maximum temperature at 4S1 /4S4 is exceeded.%CrLf%Cooling defective or temperature set too low;Check temperature settings. Check air conditioning unit.
365;26;%4Fuse dropped in fuse block %1;fuse dropped;Check fuse and turn back on
365;27;%4UPS mode activated. Controller will be shut down shortly.;The UPS is not supplied with 24 V anymore, that is the controller is only still buffered by the UPS.;After voltage recovery, the control system restarts automatically.%CrLf%If necessary, a restart of the control system is necessary, if the SPC was not yet ready or pending error messages had not yet been acknowledged during the previous control system restart.
365;28;%4UPS buffer time elapsed, control system is shut down;The 24V power supply of the control system and UPS have failed and the buffer time of the UPS has been exceeded.;24V supply of the UPS and the control system.%CrLf%After voltage recovery, the control system automatically restarts.
365;29;%4The 24 V power supply for emergency purging equipment isn't operational;The power supply of the emergency purging equipment reports an error. Battery and/or conservation charge faulty;Check power supply and replace if necessary
365;30;%4Fan %1 of RCMP cabinet is disturbed.;One of the colling fans of the RCMP cabinet is faulty.;- Check the temperature RCMP cabinet. Is it possible to intake enough cooling air?%CrLf%- Replace RPC controller.
365;31;%4The configuration parameter %1 must be activated for RCMP2 cabinets.;Using RCMP2-Cabinet this function observes the actual temperatur inside the cabinet and gives an alarm if temperature exeeds maximum.;Check configuration and restart control.
366;1;%4The control is stopped after a fatal error. ;Control was stopped due to a fatal error!;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
