393;64;%4Invalid set value %1 for %2. Allowed %3 ;The device required value lies outside of the permissible area.;Adjust override or required value for this device.
393;65;%4Counter card for device %1 is disturbed (signal %2);- Cabling error (wire break)%CrLf%- Counter card defective;- Check cabling between counter card and transmitter%CrLf%- Reset counter card by interrupting the power supply%CrLf%- Replace counter card
393;67;%4Counter card for SolventCan must be referenced again;Power loss%CrLf%- Pins at the counter card damaged%CrLf%- EMC;Reference the SolventCan via HMI interface
393;68;%4Cable break or loss of the magnetic coupling at foil potentiometer %1 (signal %2);- Loss of the magnetic coupling between piston and foil potentiometer by too fast piston movement%CrLf%- Foil potentiometer damaged%CrLf%- Defect on the connecting cable between R/O converter and foil potentiometer;- Execute referencing procedure for affected device in operation mode manual%CrLf%- Exchange foil potentiometer%CrLf%- Check cable between R/O-converter and foil potentiometer
393;168;%4Learning conveyor was canceled because conveyor is moving backward.;The function to measure in the conveyor was activated via the vision system, %CrLf%the conveyor runs backwards, however. Therefore, the calibration procedure was aborted.;Check cabling of the conveyor and start calibrating procedure once again.
