394;1;%4Velocity for conveyor filter (Conv_Vel_max) too small. Must be bigger than %1. ;In the cfg file corresponding to the FU, a speed must be entered for the filter of the incremental transmitter. This value was selected too small, however.;Check and adapt the parameters for the conveyor filter (Conv_Vel_max, Conv_Acc_max) in the cfg file corresponding to the FU.
394;2;%4Velocity for conveyor filter (Conv_Vel_max) too small for real conveyor velocity. ;In the cfg file corresponding to the FU, a speed must be entered for the filter of the incremental transmitter. This value was selected too small, however.;Check and adapt the parameters for the conveyor filter (Conv_Vel_max, Conv_Acc_max) in the cfg file corresponding to the FU.
396;1;%4Invalid channel error issued in channel %1.;Internal control problem, programming error or parameterizing error.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
396;2;%4Invalid acknowledge request for message %1 of function unit %2;The acknowledging of messages is allowed only from the functional unit SCU;Send error message as well as all necessary protocols for the error analysis to controller supplier.
396;3;%4External station stop triggered;An external station stop was triggered by the PLC;Acknowledge pending errors at the control panel / PLC
396;4;%4External station stop triggered;An external station stop was triggered by the PLC;Acknowledge pending errors at the control panel / PLC
396;5;%4Invalid error issued in channel %1.;Internal control problem, programming error or parameterizing error.;Get in contact with control supplier.
396;10;%4Control is stopped after a fatal error. ;Internal control error (division by zero, invalid array accesses, etc.);Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
396;11;%4Control is stopped because of a firmware error. ;A difficult error of class 3 was issued by the firmware. Then the control must be stopped.;- Check error at the HMI and teach pendant %CrLf%- restart control %CrLf%- if error is not found, prepare status report, remove protocols and send to control supplier together with the application%CrLf%
396;12;%4Faulty cooling fan of RPC controller.;One of the colling fans of the rpc controller is faulty.;- Check the temperature RCMP cabinet. Is it possible to intake enough cooling air?%CrLf%- Replace RPC controller.
396;13;%4Bios-Buffer-Battery of RPC controller is empty or defect.;The internal battery of the RPC controller gives too low voltage level.%CrLf%This means the battery is worn or defect.;Replace RPC controller.
396;14;%4The temperature of the RPC controller reached the warning limit.;- Temperature of RCMP cabinet too high.%CrLf%- Cooling fan dirty or faulty.%CrLf%- Ventilation grid of controller blocked.;- Check cooling device of RPC cabinet.%CrLf%- Check ventilation paths of RPC controller.
396;15;%4The temperature of the RPC controller reached the critical limit.;- Temperature of RCMP cabinet too high.%CrLf%- Cooling fan dirty or faulty.%CrLf%- Ventilation grid of controller blocked.;- Check cooling device of RPC cabinet.%CrLf%- Check ventilation paths of RPC controller.
