481;4;%4Syntax error when reading the file %1 - invalid section (line: %2);When reading the specified file a syntax error has been found in the corresponding line. This includes:%CrLf%- invalid string%CrLf%- missing entries;Check the specified file and correct the error in the corresponding line.%CrLf%Acknowledge the error.
481;5;%4Syntax error when reading the file %1 - invalid parameter key (line: %2);When reading the specified file a syntax error has been found in the corresponding line. This includes:%CrLf%- invalid string%CrLf%- missing entries;Check the specified file and correct the error in the corresponding line.%CrLf%Acknowledge the error.
481;6;%4The file %1 doesn't exist.;The stated file is not existing.;Create the stated file with 3DOnSite and save it.
481;7;%4The file %1 couldn't be deleted.;Error while deleting the stated file.;Make storage space on target volume, acknowledge error report and carry out function once again.
481;8;%4Error while moving the file %1 to %2.;The stated file couldn't be copied.;Make storage space on target volume, acknowledge error report and carry out function once again.
481;9;%4The parameter %1 of the section %2 is not existing in the file %3.;The stated parameter is not existing for the stated section in the stated file, also it is defined as relevant in the according definition file.;Check stated file and according definition file, change file with 3DOnSite and save it.
481;10;%4The data of the file %1 couldn't be read.;The data of the stated file couldn't be read.;Check stated file and according definition file, change file with 3DOnSite and save it.
481;11;%4The data of the file %1 couldn't be read.;The data of the stated file couldn't be read.;Check stated file and according definition file, change file with 3DOnSite and save it.
481;12;%4The parameter %1 isn't included in the configuration file.;The stated parameter couldn't be read.;Check configuration file and reload with 3DOnSite.
483;1;%4The parameter '%2' in File '%1' contains a format error.;;
483;2;%4KMEM-Error %1 on Position %2;;
484;1;%4KMEM-Error %1 on Position %2;;
484;2;%4The already installed parameter '%1.%2' should be installed anew with '%3';;
484;3;%4Parameter '%1' in file '%2' is not of the type %3;;
484;4;%4No Userlist-Handle has been set while initialising the parameter '%1.%2' ;;
484;6;%4In function unit %2 an uninitialised parameter of type %1 is read.;;
484;7;%4Parameter '%1.%2' was read before the initialisation.;;
484;8;%4Parameter '%1.%2' was not found.;;
484;9;%4Parameter '%1.%2' (optional to %3) was not found.;;
484;10;%4Errors while reading configuration file -virtualwall.cfg-, the boot-up of controller stopped.;- Not all requested parameters were found in configuration file.%CrLf%- Parameter in the configuration file has not the requested data type.%CrLf%- Configuration file is missing.;- Check configuration file with the windows explorer.%CrLf%- Respect detailed error output in the ProcessProtocol and correct them if necessary.
486;1;%4Getting reference to variable %1 failed.;Projectspecific function (Engineering folder) tries to access a system variable which isn't existing.%CrLf%Possible reasons for this fault: Missing device, missing fixed position etc.;Check why system variable isn't accessable%CrLf%1. Device is missing in ProcessBuilder-Project%CrLf%2. Fixed position isn't assigned in ProcessBuilder-Project.%CrLf%3. Project specific function isn't correct.
490;4;%4Initialization of ethercat slave with invalid name %1;The name of EtherCAT device differs between the process configuration and the EtherCAT configuration. This is not allowed.;Check configuration and/or device name and correct where appropriate.
490;8;%4EtherCAT device %1 is not connected.;Communication between the two participants is interrupted%CrLf%- Defective or fault in the electrical connection%CrLf%- Fault in the socket for EtherCat communication on one or both nodes;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
490;9;%4Errors while reading ethercat configuration node: %1, file %2.;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check the indicated file in the Explorer.
490;10;%4Read error EtherCat configuration parameter: %1, file %2;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check the indicated file in the Explorer.
490;12;%4No access to signal %1 of device %2.;It was attempted to reference to the indicated variable with the command GET_REFTO. This failed. Causes: bug, internal control problem.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
490;13;%4There are more EtherCat participants configured as allowed (%1).;Internal system error or system memory error.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
490;14;%4Cross-communication fault between drive controllers. Power Reset necessary!;Cross-communication between drive controllers is disturbed after an communication fault.;- check network connection to device and power reset the drive package (fuse in cabinet or main switch to power reset cabinet)
490;15;%4Configuration of cyclic drive data faulty.;The cyclic process data of the drive controllers are incomplete or incorrectly configured;- Check the configuration of the cyclic process data in KeStudio Manager --> Expert process data%CrLf%- Check whether the configured process data are mapped to the drives%CrLf%- VELOC: Actual velocity%CrLf%- AUX0: DriveID (only on the first axis of each controller)%CrLf%- AUX1: Configurable control word%CrLf%- AUX2: Motor temperature%CrLf%- AUX3: Encoder temperature
490;16;%4Bootup of controller interrupted because drive %1 is not operational.;Drive fault.%CrLf%Communication fault with drive.%CrLf%Power supply of drive or drive controller not ok.;Check if mentioned drive has any faults.%CrLf%Check EtherCAT communication to drive.%CrLf%Check power supply of drive.
490;17;%4 Supply voltage %1 of motor holding brake out of range (%2) measured at EncoderBox %3.;- Fault in wiring: Supply voltage of EncoderBox faulty.%CrLf%- Hardware defect: Power supply damaged.%CrLf%- Wrong adjustment: The adjusted voltage of the power supply is not correct.;- Please check the electrical wiring.%CrLf%- Check the power supply and exchange if it's damaged.%CrLf%- Verify adjusted voltage of power supply.
490;20;%4Overtemperature robot control %3 (%1°C > %2°C);- Fan defect or heavily dirty%CrLf%- Temperature in cabinet to high%CrLf%- Temperature sensor defect;- Check fans of control and rcmp cabinet%CrLf%- Check intake of cooling air%CrLf%- Replace control
490;21;%4Overtemperature supply unit %3 (%1°C > %2°C);- Fan defect or heavily dirty%CrLf%- Temperature in cabinet to high%CrLf%- Temperature sensor defect;- Check fans of control and rcmp cabinet%CrLf%- Check intake of cooling air%CrLf%- Replace control
490;22;%4Overtemperature drive controller %3 (%1°C > %2°C);- Fan defect or heavily dirty%CrLf%- Temperature in cabinet to high%CrLf%- Temperature sensor defect;- Check fans of control and rcmp cabinet%CrLf%- Check intake of cooling air%CrLf%- Replace control
490;99;%4EtherCAT device %1 is not connected.;Communication between the two participants is interrupted%CrLf%- Defective or fault in the electrical connection%CrLf%- Fault in the socket for EtherCat communication on one or both nodes;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
491;1;%4Serial number of the drive controller or encoder %1 couldn't be read.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;2;%4 Name of motor of drive %1 couldn't be read.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;3;%4 Encoder offset of drive %1 couldn't be read.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;4;%Firmware version of the drive controller %1 couldn't be read.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;5;%4New serial number of the drive controller %1 identified, motor data are loaded.;- Exchange of device.%CrLf%- Restore backup of the flash with 3D-OnSite.%CrLf%- Communication fault with device.;Wait a short time until motor data are loaded and quit message.
491;6;%4New serial number of the motor %1 identified, motor data are loaded.;- Exchange of device.%CrLf%- Restore backup of the flash with 3D-OnSite.%CrLf%- Communication fault with device.;Wait a short time until motor data are loaded and quit message.
491;7;%4Changed motor parametrisation of the motor %1 identified, motor data are loaded.;- Drive parameters were loaded.%CrLf%- Restore backup of the flash with 3D-OnSite.%CrLf%- Communication fault with device.;Wait a short time until motor data are loaded and quit message.
491;8;%4Motor data of %1 are loaded.;- Exchange of device.%CrLf%- Drive parameters were loaded.%CrLf%- Restore backup of the flash with 3D-OnSite.%CrLf%- Communication fault with device.;Wait a short time until motor data are loaded and quit message.
491;9;%4Parameter file of motor %1 couldn't be loaded.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;10;%4Parameter file of motor %1 couldn't be interpreted.;The data of the stated file couldn't be read.;Shutdown controller %CrLf%Powercycle device %CrLf%Restart controller
491;11;%4Parameter file of motor %1 has invalid checksum.;- The parameter file is corrupt.%CrLf%- Encoder memory is defect.%CrLf%- The checksum of the parameter file doesn't match with the file content.;Shutdown controller %CrLf%Powercycle device %CrLf%Restart controller
491;12;%4Mounted motor %1 isn't compatible.;Mounted motor type isn't the same type than previous mounted.%CrLf%Mounted motor type doesn't match with configured standard motor type.%CrLf%Mounted motor type isn't compatible with configured standard motor type.%CrLf%;Mount an electrical compatible motor.%CrLf%Check configuration of standard motor type.
491;13;%4Firmware version %1 of drive controller is too old for mounted motor %2 (min. FW=%3).;Firmware version of drive controller is too old for mounted motor. A firmware version equal or higher than mentioned version is required to run connected motor.;- Update firmware of drive controller.%CrLf%- Exchange drive controller with a newer one.%CrLf%- Mount another drive.
491;14;%4Parameter file of motor %1 couldn't be processed.;- Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.%CrLf%- The parameter file is corrupt.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;15;%4Parameter file of motor %1 contains no data.;- The parameter file is corrupt.%CrLf%- Encoder memory is defect.%CrLf%- The checksum of the parameter file doesn't match with the file content.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;16;%4Loading data of motor %1 successful finished.;User information;Acknowledge fault
491;17;%4No standardmotor for drive %1 found in configuration.;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check and correct configuration, then restart control.
491;18;%4Entry motor name not found in parameter file of motor %1.;- The parameter file is corrupt.%CrLf%- Encoder memory is defect.%CrLf%- The checksum of the parameter file doesn't match with the file content.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;19;%4Entry firmware version not found in parameter file of motor %1.;- The parameter file is corrupt.%CrLf%- Encoder memory is defect.%CrLf%- The checksum of the parameter file doesn't match with the file content.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;20;%4Encoder memory of motor %1 contains too many objects. Maximum amount %2.;Internal system error or system memory error.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
491;21;%4Mounted motor %1 isn't compatible to drive controller %2 and it's parametrisation.;Wrong parametrisation of drive controller.;Load correct parameters in the drive controller.
491;22;%4Bootup stopped. It was not possible to access all drive controllers.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;23;%4Bootup stopped. Parameter (%2) couldn't be read from drive %1.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
491;24;%4The drive configuration has been modified by the controller, powercycling requested!;For correct operating of the robot drives some specified parameters have to be modified by the controller.;To activate the changed parameters the RCMP cabinet has to be powercycled by main switch.
496;7;%4Participant with address %2 was detected at position %1 instead of the configured participants with address %3;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
496;8;%4Sercos device %1 is not connected.;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
496;9;%4Errors while reading sercos configuration node: %1, file %2.;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check the indicated file in the Explorer.
496;10;%4Errors while reading sercos configuration parameter: %1, file %2.;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check the indicated file in the Explorer.
496;12;%4No access to signal %1 of device %2.;It was attempted to reference to the indicated variable with the command GET_REFTO. This failed. Causes: bug, internal control problem.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
496;13;%4More sercos devices in configuration than allowed (%1);Internal system error or system memory error.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
496;14;%4Found wrong/unknown sercos device with address %2 at position %1.;- Found device address which is not configured.%CrLf%- More device connected than configured.%CrLf%- Faulty device.;- Compare bus installation with electrical drawing. %CrLf%- Check device and power cycle it if necessary.
496;15;%4Communication of sercos ring is disturbed.;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check of the connection and exchange where appropriate%CrLf%- Check of Sercos 3 components and exchange where appropriate
496;16;%4Sercos connection between device %1 and %2 is disturbed.;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check of the connection and exchange where appropriate%CrLf%- Check of Sercos 3 components and exchange where appropriate
496;17;%4Found simulated sercos device with address=%2 at position %1.;Found sercos device on bus system which is simulated in the configuration, this is not allowed.;Check and correct configuration, then restart control.
496;18;%4Bootup of controller interrupted, there are %1 sercos devices configured but %2 detected.;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
496;19;%4No corresponding machine for drive %1 found.;In the name of the drive the name of corresponding machine has to be included.;Clarify why one or both parameters were entered into the configuration with different values.
496;20;%4Phase change interrupted, errors in bus topologie detected (follow other messages).;- Found device address which is not configured.%CrLf%- More device connected than configured.%CrLf%- Faulty device.;- Compare bus installation with electrical drawing. %CrLf%- Check device and power cycle it if necessary.
496;21;%4Reinitialisation of Sercos 3 bussystem is active.;Errors occured while bootup of Sercos 3 Bussystem which stopped the bootup. Because of that the controller started reinitialisation of Sercos-Bussystem.;Quit error message and wait if bussystem is able startup after reinitialisation. Otherwise consider futher messages and clear errors.
496;22;%4Sercos bootup stopped because set/actual comparison is configured.;In sercosconfiguration "autoAddressing=2" is assigned. This is only for commissioning purpose (Set/actual comparision) with keStudio valid.;After commissioning set parameter "autoAddressing=3" in sercosconfiguration and restart controller.
496;23;%4Sercos boot up not possible due to other faults, power cycle devices.;Errors happened which do not allow to boot up sercos.;- Power cycle Sercosdevices, when devices have rebooted then restart Sercosring. - Please check further messages of devices. - Check power supply as well as wiring of the devices.
496;24;%4Please execute Sercos restart to establish communication with all devices.;Not all Sercos devices are communicating with the Sercos master.%CrLf%These devices are now reachable by network. To reestablish communication please restart Sercos ring.;Wait for gap between bodies, if neseccary lock inlet and execute Sercos restart on HMI.
496;25;%4Error in sercos3 configuration: traceWord not set;Sercos3 configuration faulty. Traceword must be set correctly (traceWord=16) for error analysis;Check and correct sercos3 configuration.
496;26;%4Error in sercos configuration: resetStartupErrors not set;Sercos3 configuration with errors: option to quit errors during bootup must be set (resetStartupErrors=1);Check and correct sercos3 configuration.
496;98;%4Sercos device %1 is not connected.;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
496;99;%4Sercos device %1 is not connected.;Communication interruption between two Secos 3 components%CrLf%- Defect of the electrical connection between the two components%CrLf%- Defect of the interface for Sercos 3 bus communication of one or of both components%CrLf%;- Check device, power cycle device. %CrLf%- Check the electrical connection (sequential arrangement, plugs).%CrLf%
496;100;%4Network settings have been changed on device %1. To activate these settings the device has to be power cycled.;To activate the changed settings of the device it has to be power cycled.;- Remove all power from device.%CrLf%- Restore supply voltage.%CrLf%- Restart S3 bus.
496;102;%4Unable to read the network settings of device %1.;Errors while reading the network parameters.;- Remove all power from device.%CrLf%- Restore supply voltage.%CrLf%- Restart S3 bus.
496;103;%4Unable to write network settings to device %1.;Errors while writing network parameters to device.;- Remove all power from device.%CrLf%- Restore supply voltage.%CrLf%- Restart S3 bus.
496;104;%4Unable to activate the network settings on device %1.;Errors occured while activating the network parameters.;- Remove all power from device.%CrLf%- Restore supply voltage.%CrLf%- Restart S3 bus.
496;105;%4Topology check is activated but parameter %1 is not activated. This not allowed.;Mentioned parameter has value = 0 in configuration. Only value = 1 is allowed. This parameter activates the startup of the application even the topologycheck has not detected all configured devices. ;Check configuration and restart control.
496;106;%4Parameter %1 has invalid value %2, requested value %3.;The value of this configuration parameter doesn't fit with requested value.;Check configuration and restart control.
496;110;%4The system time for actuator %1 could not be read.;Error while reading system time (P-0-0197);In the device documentation, check whether the parameter exists.%CrLf%Check the communication.%CrLf%Restart device.
496;111;%4The system time for actuator %1 could not be written.;Error while writing system time (P-0-0197);In the device documentation, check whether the parameter exists.%CrLf%Check the communication.%CrLf%Restart device.
496;112;%4error ex-contactor;Information from the station PLC that the EX-protection was switched off;Check whether the robot is sealed. Wait until the robot is rinsed
496;201;%4The number or order of the modules on the device %1 do not correspond to the configuration.;- The number of modules doesn't match the configuration%CrLf%- The module types found do not correspond to the configuration e.g (AI instead of AI-T)%CrLf%- The order of the modules doesn't match the configuration;- Reset power supply of the device and restart the control%CrLf%- Start diagnosis by checking the LED at the gateway and on the modules%CrLf% - Phoenix: LED at the upper edge of the module indicating connection to the gateway%CrLf%    - Check power supply%CrLf%    - Check connection of the module at the back plane bus%CrLf%    - Exchange the module%CrLf%  - Festo: Modules have a CTEI LED indicating connection to the gateway%CrLf%    - LED off: Check wiring, connector, exchange the module%CrLf%    - LED blinking: Check module type and order%CrLf%A reset of the modules power supply as well as a reset of the robot controller is required after any change
496;202;%4Sercos slave %1 signalize defect valve unit (VTOM);Inconsistence between parametrized and found FESTO valve unit%CrLf%- hardware config faulty or wrong valve unit used%CrLf%- one or more valve blocks defect;Check hardware configuration and type of used valve unit. If check is ok, then replace the complete valve unit.
497;2;%4Voltage supply of the motor holding brake drive %1 is below the permissible limit.;The supply voltage of the motor holding brake is below the permitted value for which there may be several causes:%CrLf% - Wiring error: At the analog input of the drive controller an incorrect voltage was applied.%CrLf% - Hardware defect: The circuit board for the voltage divider is damaged.%CrLf% - Parameterization error: The voltage set on the power supply device is too low.;- Please check the electrical wiring.%CrLf%- Check the electrical circuit board and exchange if it's damaged.%CrLf%- Verify adjusted voltage of power supply.
497;3;%4Error at GET_REFTO on variable %1 in device %2;It was attempted to reference to the indicated variable with the command GET_REFTO. This failed. Causes: bug, internal control problem.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
497;4;%4Initialisation of sercos device with invalid name %1.;The name of mentioned sercos device is not the same in process-/ and sercos configuration. This is not allowed.;Check configuration and/or device name and correct where appropriate.
497;5;%4No access to sercos device %1.;It was attempted to reference to the indicated variable with the command GET_REFTO. This failed. Causes: bug, internal control problem.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
497;9;%4Device %1 supports %2 function but neither SCP_Sync nor Watchdog is configured.;To recognize Master failures secos devices need the SCP_Sync or Watchdog function. The sercos device sets it's signal levels to default value when master fault were detected. In this case the device supports the function but it's not configured.;Verify the sercos configuration or contact controller manufacturer.
497;10;%4Supply voltage of motor holding brake drive %1 is above upper bound.;- Fault in wiring: Wrong supply voltage is connected to the analog input of the drive controller.%CrLf%- Hardware defect: Circuit board of voltage divider is damaged.%CrLf%- Wrong adjustment: The adjusted voltage of the power supply is too high.;- Please check the electrical wiring.%CrLf%- Check the electrical circuit board and exchange if it's damaged.%CrLf%- Verify adjusted voltage of power supply.
497;2000;%4%1 Invalid handle for Sercos device %2;The device is not included in the bus configuration or a wrong device name was indicated.;Check configuration and/or device name and correct where appropriate.
497;2002;%4No Sercos III framework could be determined for the HW terminal point %1.;No Sercos III device could be determined for the so-called HW terminal point. The HW terminal point is possibly%CrLf% not integrated in the Sercos III configuration.;Sercos III configuration, check HW terminal point name
497;2100;%4%1 Reading of parameter %2 failed.;The parameter is not existing in the device.%CrLf%The communication to the device is interrupted.%CrLf%The device does not react to service channel accesses;In the device documentation, check whether the parameter exists.%CrLf%Check the communication.%CrLf%Restart device.
497;2200;%4%1 Writing of parameter %2 failed.;The parameter is not existing in the device.%CrLf%The communication to the device is interrupted.%CrLf%The device does not react to service channel accesses;In the device documentation, check whether the parameter exists.%CrLf%Check the communication.%CrLf%Restart device.
497;2901;%4Hardware end point %1 not functional.;Miswiring or hardware defect. %CrLf%Communication fault or bus failure.;
497;2902;%4Hardware error (device: %1, module %2, channel %3);Miswiring or hardware defect. %CrLf%Communication fault or bus failure.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
497;2903;%4the drive %1 which is configured to supervise the break voltage, could not be found;The voltage of the motor holding brake must be monitored for at least one drive controller.%CrLf%This is done by connecting the brake voltage at the analog input of the first drive controller and the inclusion of the value (P-0-0210) in the cyclic channel.%CrLf%If the parameter (P-0-0210) could not be found on any of the drive controllers' cyclic channel, so this error message will be shown;Check the parametrization of the drive configuration and clarify why P-0-0210 is not contained in the cyclic channel.
497;2904;%4communication error device %1;Miswiring or hardware defect. %CrLf%Communication fault or bus failure.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
497;2905;%4Power supply of motor brake axis %1 has no voltage 0V.; - Error at the electrical connection of the voltage divider.%CrLf% - The parameter (P-0-0210 ) is not configured in the cyclic data channel.;- Check electrical connection and drive-/ controller configuration as well.
497;2906;%4Communication error device %1;Miswiring or hardware defect. %CrLf%Communication fault or bus failure.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
497;2907;%4Error reading parameter %1 from %2 for supervising the break voltage.;The parameter is not existing in the device.%CrLf%The communication to the device is interrupted.%CrLf%The device does not react to service channel accesses;In the device documentation, check whether the parameter exists.%CrLf%Check the communication.%CrLf%Restart device.
497;2908;%4Communication error device %1;Miswiring or hardware defect. %CrLf%Communication fault or bus failure.;* Check wiring and hardware.%CrLf%* Check status of superordinate modules.%CrLf%* Check communication of bus.%CrLf%* Restart hardware and/or bus if necessary.%CrLf%* Restart control, contact control manufacturer if necessary.
497;2910;%4Problems while initialization of device %1. Please power cycle device.;- Festo I/O module was changed without power cycling device. - Configuration of I/O Module doesn't fit with hardware installtion. - Restart of local bus (CTEI) failed.;- Power cycle mentioned device and restart RPC afterwards. - Compare configuration of Sercosbus with hardware installation.
497;3001;%4%1 unknown error (code: %2);The device has issued an unknown error code. Possibly a device with newer firmware state was installed.;Check device documentation.%CrLf%Possibly contact controller manufacturer.%CrLf%
497;3910;%4Problems while initialization of device %1 because module %2 not detected.;- Festo I/O module was changed without power cycling device. - Configuration of I/O Module doesn't fit with hardware installtion. - Restart of local bus (CTEI) failed.;- Power cycle mentioned device and restart RPC afterwards. - Compare configuration of Sercosbus with hardware installation.
497;4001;%4%1 Unknown warning (code: %2);The device has issued an unknown error code. Possibly a device with newer firmware state was installed.;Check device documentation.%CrLf%Possibly contact controller manufacturer.%CrLf%
497;4100;%4%1 Reading of parameter %2 failed.;The parameter is not existing in the device.%CrLf%The communication to the device is interrupted.%CrLf%The device does not react to service channel accesses;In the device documentation, check whether the parameter exists.%CrLf%Check the communication.%CrLf%Restart device.
497;4910;%4Problems while initialization of device %1 because module %2 not detected.;- Festo I/O module was changed without power cycling device. - Configuration of I/O Module doesn't fit with hardware installtion. - Restart of local bus (CTEI) failed.;- Power cycle mentioned device and restart RPC afterwards. - Compare configuration of Sercosbus with hardware installation.
498;1;%4Device %1 cfg selector is neither 1 nor 2, but %2. ;Control was stopped due to a fatal error!;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
