499;4610;%4Air check paint canister 1 triggered. Program %1, step %2, %3;1. Air bubbles from ring pipe%CrLf%2. Air bubbles in paint caused by leaky valves PL1 or QL1BL1%CrLf%3. Airseal at piston in painting canister defective;1.1 Check flow riser for air bubbles%CrLf%1.2. Drain color an restart the process again%CrLf%2.1 Check valve PL1 for leakage by using pressure sensor in color changer (pressure increase?)%CrLf%2.2 Check valve QL1BL1 by opening valve QL1F1, check if pressure is increasing in color changer%CrLf%2.3 Dismount painting canister 1 and exchange piston
499;4611;%4Air check paint canister 2 triggered. Program %1, step %2, %3;1. Air bubbles from painting canister 1 during loading or refilling%CrLf%2. Valve ZL2BL1 leaky%CrLf%3. Air seal of piston in painting canister 2 defective;1. Check preloading sequence, if time is sufficient%CrLf%2. Open valves ZL2BL1 and ZL2F1, release pressure in CAN2 and observe if filling level is increasing%CrLf%3. Dismount painting canister 2 and exchange piston
499;4612;%4Pressure in color changer too low at the current color. Program %1, step %2, %3;1. Pressure in ring pipe too low%CrLf%2. Contamination in color valve%CrLf%3. Defective valve in color changer%CrLf%4. Pneumatic control of color valve defective;1. Check pressure in ring pipe / increase%CrLf%2. Remove contamination in color valve%CrLf%3. Exchange color valve in color changer%CrLf%4. Check pneumatic activation
499;4613;%4Solvent pressure too low during referencing. Prog. %1, Step %2, %3;1. Feeding line of medium faulty. (Shut-off valve, ball valve etc. closed)%CrLf%2. Parameter for minimum flow selected too large%CrLf%3. Check pneumatic activation;Check process components.%CrLf%
499;4614;%4Leackage check of entire system done without error;Leak check of the entire system performed without error;None
499;4615;%4 Error pressure increase during leakage test prog. %1, step %2, %3;Leaking valves for air or solvent%CrLf%Leaking piston of paint canister 1 or 2;- Check valves and replace in case of a defect%CrLf%- Check piston and replace in case of a defect
499;4616;%4 Error pressure reduction during leakage test prog. %1, step %2, %3;Leakage in the system;Check all valves, seals, interfaces
499;4617;%4 Timeout while relieving pressure during pressure check for puls air. Prog %1, step %2, %3;- Valve RF2 doesn't open%CrLf%- Valves PL1 or V1 leaky;- Check valves RF2, PL1, V1
499;4618;%4Pressure regulator for puls air 1 is not set properly. Prog %1, step %2, %3;- Pressure regulator for puls air 1 in arm1 is not set correctly%CrLf%- Valve RF2 leaky;- Set pressure regulator for puls air 1 in arm1 properly. Procedure: see manual%CrLf%- Check valve RF2
499;4619;%4V1 solvent pressure too low during purging. Prog. %1, Step %2, %3;- Pressure regulator VV1 is not adjusted correctly%CrLf%- Solvent tube dissolved or kinked%CrLf%- Valve V1 defective or does not switch%CrLf%- Control for valve V1 defective%CrLf%- Valve RF2 leaking;- Adjust pressure regulator VV1%CrLf%- Check solvent tube to color changer%CrLf%- Check function of valve V1%CrLf%- Check control for valve V1%CrLf%- Check if valve RF2 is leaking
499;4620;%4QL1BL1 air pressure too low during purging. Prog. %1, Step %2, %3;- Pressure regulator in arm1 not adjusted correctly%CrLf%- Tube for air pressure supply dissolved or kinked%CrLf%- Valve QL1BL1 defective or does not switch%CrLf%- Control for valve QL1BL1 defective;- Adjust pressure regulator in arm1%CrLf%- Check the air supply hose to valve QL1BL1%CrLf%- Check function of valve QL1BL1%CrLf%- Check control for valve QL1BL1
499;4621;%4ZL2V1 solvent pressure too low during purging. Prog. %1, Step %2, %3;- Pressure regulator QVV1 is not adjusted correctly%CrLf%- Solvent supply  in the area of insulating cylinder V interrupted%CrLf%- Solvent tube dissolved or kinked%CrLf%- Valve ZL2V1 defective or does not switch%CrLf%- Control for valve ZL2V1 defective;- Adjust pressure regulator QVV1 in color niche%CrLf%- Check solvent supply through insulating cylinder V possibly blocked by any object%CrLf%- Check solvent supply tube to valve station CAN2%CrLf%- Check function of valve ZL2V1%CrLf%- Check control for valve ZL2V1%CrLf%
499;4622;%4ZL2BL1 solvent pressure too low during purging. Prog. %1, Step %2, %3;- Pressure regulator in arm1 is not adjusted correctly%CrLf%- Air supply tube dissolved or kinked%CrLf%- Valve ZL2BL1 defective or does not switch%CrLf%- Control for valve ZL2BL1 defective%CrLf%;- Adjust pressure regulator in arm1%CrLf%- Check the air supply hose to valve ZL2BL1%CrLf%- Check function of valve ZL2BL1%CrLf%- Check control for valve ZL2BL1
