503;14;%4Handler cannot be started because no access to field bus ;Not all inputs/outputs of the field bus slave could be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware end points in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%one or several inputs/outputs were not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
503;15;%4SET_POSCODE was executed with new part position without deleting the current part position.;Before a handler moves the part the current part position has to be deleted with the command SET_POSCODE(Delete). This ensures that other robots don't get a wrong part position while the part is moved. ;Before the part is moved by a handler the command SET_POSCODE(Delete) has to executed. Please check current EcoTalk programm.
503;16;%4Error shutting down high tension for incomming handler order;Ecotalk command to shut down high tension was set but process part doesn' t provide the necessary information;Internal control error, deselect robot and contact control manufacturer.
503;17;%4In Ecotalk program line %1 the command to receive a handling order is programmed without switching off high tension before;The EcoTalk command for reading handling tasks has been executed without switching off the high tension before. This is not allowed%CrLf%- fire hazard by high tension flashover;The high tension must be shut down with command "SET_PROCESS_STATE" before "RECEIVE_PARTORDER" is executed.
503;18;%4It's only allowed the switch on high tension with destined handling order - Program line %1.;EcoTalk command "SET_PROCESS_STATE" was executed without using the destined handling order. This isn't allowed - fire danger caused by high tension trip;The EcoTalk command "RECEIVE_PARTORDER" has to be used to release the high tension before the high tension can be released by using the EcoTalk command "SET_PROCESS_STATE".
503;19;%4It isn't allowed to release high tension - handling is active "RECEIVE_ORDER" is executed- Program line %1.;EcoTalk command "SET_PROCESS_STATE" to release high tension is executed but robot is handling mode at the moment. Command "RECEIVE_ORDER" is executed. This isn't allowed - fire danger caused by high tension trip;Pleas check the EcoTalk sub-programs whitch are used by handling tasks.%CrLf%In this sub-programs the EcoTalk command "SET_PROCESS_STATE" must not be used to release the high tension.
