513;37;%4No access to actual value of drive %1 for %2 ;It was attempted to map the readback values of the drive, this did not succeed.%CrLf%Internal control problem or the use of the readback values is not configured.;Check configuration and restart control.
513;38;%4No access to set value of drive %1 for %2 ;It was attempted to map the actJointPosition of the drive, this did not succeed.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
513;39;%4Detection of standstill monitoring axis %1 has reacted.;The actual value of the concerned axis has changed without a required value having been pre-set.;Eliminate external influence
513;40;%4Detection of position monitoring axis %1 has reacted. ;The concerned drives did not reach its standstill position within the preset time.;Relieve robot if jammed.
513;41;%4No access to input %1 of axis limit switch drive: %2. ;The mentioned hardware endpoint could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware end points in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input/output was not created or several inputs/outputs in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with circuit diagram, then restart control.
513;43;%4Internal error or error in configuration. %1 cannot be mapped;Control was stopped due to a fatal error!;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
513;44;%4Drive %1: Motor type differs from configured motor type;Motor type differs from configured motor type.;Check motor type.
513;45;%4The maximum axis velocity of %1 must not exceed %2.;The maximum stopping time (maxEmergencyStopTimeMs), stored in the safe configuration, requires a minor axis velocitiy than the configured.;The configured axis velocity (maxVelo, in MachineDataX.cfg) must not be higher than the displayed value.
513;46;%4The maximum axis jerk of %1 must not exceed %2.;The configured maximum axis jerk (maxJerk, in MachineDataX.cfg) is too big.;Configure maximum axis jerk to displayed value.
513;47;%4Drive %1 cound not be switched on because the safety controller does not open the brake.;Disturbance of the encoderbox or the drivecontroller.;Check further error messages and eleminate them if necessary.
513;48;%4Encoder offset=%1 of drive %2 has changed. (Origin value %3). Restart robot controller !;Now parameters were loaded to the drive controller.;The new loaded parameters have overwritten the motor specific data.%CrLf%This specific data must be relaoded from the motor. Perform restart of the robort controller to reload the motor data.
513;49;%4New motor at %1 detected, Restart robot controller !;The serial number of the motor encoder has changed. Another motor was connected.%CrLf%The parameters from the motor name plate must be transmitted to drive controller.;Restart RPC-controller.
513;50;%4 %1 not ready for operation.;- connection to DC-link defective%CrLf%- encoder connection faulty%CrLf%- invalid parameters;- check connection to DC-link%CrLf%- check encoder connection%CrLf%- check parameters
513;51;%4Incorrect input voltage in the drive supply unit;Too large deviations of the voltages between the 3 phases have been measured at the input of the supply unit.;Check electrical installation.
