540;21;%4Mastering aborted because drives are not connected;During the master process, the drives were switched off, the dead man switch was released %CrLf%or other drive error.;Start master process again, pay attention to further drive errors where appropriate.%CrLf%e.g. axis limit switch and so forth.
540;22;%4Distance too small to recognize sensor signal edge for mastering axis %2;During the mastering of the specified axis, the traveling distance (mastering delta) did not suffice to detect a slope change of the sensor signal 0 -> 1.;Check cabling of the master sensor. Ensure that negative and positive feedback of the signal is recognized.%CrLf%Increase mastering delta in the configuration of the mentioned axis.
540;23;%4Error while calculating mastering offsets for hand axes ;It was attempted to change the current axis values into motor values, this did not succeed.%CrLf%Cause: Internal control problem ;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
540;24;%4Hand axis %1 mastering aborted, because axis %2 not in master position.;An attempt was made to master the specified hand axis without the complained axis standing in reference position.%CrLf%All hand axes must be mastered consecutively. Axis 4 --> 5 --> 6.;Move complained axis into reference position, master again where appropriate.
540;25;%4Target position %1 of axis %2 beyond limit %3 during automatic mastering ;The target position for the automatic mastering results from the "current position" + "masteringdelta" from the robot configuration. This is outside of the axis end, however.;Check start position for the mastering and/or start the master process on master sensor.%CrLf%if necessary, check whether the configured master path "masteringdelta" is correctly configured.
540;26;%4Function call %1 failed;Programming error or internal control problem;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
