548;29;%4Macro %1 has been ignored. SmartRay functionality has been deaktivated.;In the teach program, macros are used which cannot be processed in the control.;Either remove the macros or parameterize the SmartRay functionality in the configuration [RC.KINEMATIC:0.SmartRay].
548;30;%4Illegal table status received from the PLC.;When checking the table status, the PLC reports more than one place as not occupied.;Check table.
548;31;%4Illegal hole number received from the PLC in EcoTalk-Program Line: %1. Hole number %2 expected and hole number %3 received.;The hole number received from the PLC does not agree with the requested hole number.;Correct error in the PLC program
548;32;%4The nozzle %1 on head %2 is defect.;Nozzle defective;Repair the tool head
548;33;%4Head cannot be undocked.;The undocking of the tool could not be carried out;Check tool and docking equipment. Dock or undock tool manually
548;34;%4The tool cannot be docked.;The docking of the tool could not be carried out;Check tool and docking equipment. Dock or undock tool manually
548;35;%4For%4a BCC Macro is used in the EcoTalk-Program in Line:%1, BCC is not activated in the configuration.;Refer to error text;Check configuration and/or device name and correct where appropriate.
548;36;%4For%4, a PI macro was used in EcoTalk program line: %1, PI is not activated in the configuration, however;Configuration error;Check configuration and restart control.
548;37;%4The nozzle %1 at the head %2 is defective;Nozzle defective;Repair the tool head
548;38;%4No access to the system variable: %1 from EcoTalk command: %2, line: %3.;With an EcoTalk command, an attempt was made to access the mentioned system variable, this did not succeed.;Please check the spelling of the variable in the EcoTalk command.%CrLf%- Please check whether the variable exists in the EcoTalk command.
548;39;%4An attempt was made to set more than %1 system variables from EcoTalk.;Only the set specified number of system variables can be set in a project. An attempt was made, however, to set more than the specified number.;Check the number of system variables to be set in the motion program and reduce where appropriate.
548;40;%4EcoTalk -command - %1 - was used, but this function is not activated.;Invalid parameterization.;Check parameterization
548;41;%4, EcoTalk program line %1: No place was found to deposit the nozzle.;No place was found to deposit the nozzle.;Clear the way at the nozzle change station or remove nozzle manually from robot.
548;42;%4, EcoTalk program line %1: No nozzle of the desired type was found.;No nozzle of the desired type was found.;Insert nozzle of desired type into the nozzle change station manually.
548;43;%4, EcoTalk program line %1: The nozzle could not be deposited.;The initiator of the place of the nozzle change station is not occupied.;- Check initiator. Check %CrLf%- EcoTalk program for the depositing of the nozzle.
548;44;%4, EcoTalk program line %1: The nozzle could not be picked up.;The initiator of the place of the nozzle change station is still occupied.;- Check initiator. Check %CrLf%- EcoTalk program for the picking up of the nozzle.
548;45;%4, EcoTalk program line %1: The valve of the nozzle change station could not be switched.;Valve of the nozzle change station defective.;Check/repair valve of the nozzle exchange station.
548;46;%4Macro %1 cannot be used;In the EcoTalk program, SPLINE commands are used although they are not permissible on this controller.;Remove SPLIN commands from the EcoTalk program or allow SPLIN macros. Entry "[RC.KINEMATIC:0] enableSplineInterpolation = 1" in the RobotControl.cfg.
548;47;%4Macro %1 has been ignored. Multigun functionality has been deaktivated.;In the teach program, macros are used which cannot be processed in the control.;Either remove the macros or enter parameters for the multi-gun functionality in the configuration [RC.KINEMATIC:0.DvdGluing].
548;48;%4Macro %1 cannot be used;A EcoTalk program is using SMOOTH-path commands, but they are not available with the actual installed firmware of the robot control;Remove SMOOTH-path command from EcoTalk program or update the controler firmware
548;49;%4EcoTalk program line %1: Request if car body is fixed is only in profile free area allowed.;With the EcoTalk command "WAIT_MOTION_STATE(BodyFixation, True)" the robot is waiting until the car body is fixed. This command must be used in profile free area because of the risk of collision.;Correct EcoTalk command according to EcoTalk Doku and reload teach program.
548;50;%4EcoTalk program line %1: Command is used with wrong option %2.;This command has to used synchronously to the main run of the teachprogram otherwise it's executed too early. The robot has not reached yet the position were the command was programmed.;Correct EcoTalk command according to EcoTalk Doku and reload teach program.
548;51;%4EcoTalk command %1 can't be executed, because path correction isn't activated.;In the teach program, macros are used which cannot be processed in the control.;Either remove the macros or parameterize the path correction in the configuration [RC.KINEMATIC:0.VMT_BK].
548;52;%4In one of the movement programs of the EcoTalkProject - %1 - the command %2 is missing.;At the beginning of the movement program the requested robot must be selected and at end of the program it must be released.%CrLf%This is done with the commands RSELECT(Robotname) bzw. RDESELECT(Robotname).%CrLf%In one of the programs of the current project the mentioned command is missing.;Correct EcoTalk command according to EcoTalk Doku and reload teach program.
548;53;%4EcoTalk command %1 can't be executed, because path correction isn't activated.;In the teach program, macros are used which cannot be processed in the control.;Either remove the macros or configure the ZEISS sensor in the configuration [RC.KINEMATIC: 0.ZEISS].
548;54;%4Macro %1 may only be used in simulation.;A macro was used to simulate measured values for the Zeiss measuring computer. This macro may only be used for test purposes in simulation mode;Either delete the macro from the teach program or switch to simulation mode with the configuration entry:%CrLf%[RC.KINEMATIC:0.ZEISS]%CrLf%Simulate        = 1
549;1;%4No entry for '%1' in the configuration file (%2) ;Error or reading error of the configuration;Check configuration and restart control.
549;2;%4No access to robot configuration (%1) ;Error or reading error of the configuration;Check configuration and restart control.
549;3;%4The PB output addresses for fixed positions have not been configured completely ;Error or reading error of the configuration;Check configuration and restart control.
549;4;%4Timeout while reading the fixed position data from file %1 ;Within the defaulted time, the data of the fixed position points could not be accessed.;Check mentioned file and restart control
549;5;%4Fixed position point %1 generated by process builder and has not been taught yet ;A new fixed position was generated with the ProcessBuilder which has not been taught yet.%CrLf%Thus the coordinate system of the fixed position point is invalid and the fixed position cannot be evaluated.;Program the mentioned fixed position point with the teach pendant at adequate place and %CrLf%close and reload the project "global".
549;6;%4There is more than one position configured for fixed position %1 ;In the ProcessBuilder, more than one position was configured for profile free/deselection position ;Check configuration and restart control.
549;8;%4No access to the axis data of the kinematics %1 ;Internal control problem. It was attempted to determine the number of robot axes. The access to these data failed.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
549;9;%4The program number %1 of the fixed position %2 is not valid;The program number configured in the ProcessBuilder is not valid.;Check the program number configured in the ProcessBuilder and restart control.
549;15;%4Not all fixed position points are contained in the file '_globalvars.tid';Not all fixed position points that were configured are contained in the file _globalvars.;Check the file _globalvars and restart control.
549;16;%4The point %1 has to be taught in %2 coordinates;The stated point is programmed in the wrong coordinate system ;Program mentioned point in the demanded coordinate system and restart control
549;17;%4Read error when reading the coordinates for fixed position %1 ;The mentioned point is not contained in the file _globalvars.%CrLf%More than one point is configured as unselect/bypass/home.%CrLf%Coordinates of the point are all "zero"%CrLf%;Check _globalvars and configuration, restart control.
549;20;%4The monitoring space for %1 could not be generated because the point data of _globalvars is invalid.;The mentioned point is not contained in the file _globalvars.%CrLf%More than one point is configured as unselect/bypass/home.%CrLf%Coordinates of the point are all "zero"%CrLf%;Check _globalvars and configuration, restart control.
549;21;%4Call of the function McuCreateArea failed for working area %1. ;The call of the MCU function McuCreateArea was not successful. Read error of the data from the file _globalvars.ttp or %CrLf%internal control problem.;Check fixed position point and restart control.
549;22;%4Failed to map the appendant kinematics ;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Check configuration and restart control.
549;23;%4no size in %1 direction for %2 monitoring area configured.;In the configuration, a value for the size of the supervision space in mentioned direction %CrLf%must be configured. With adjusted robot type, a supervision must occur for this coordinate.;In the configuration file Robotcontrol.cfg, configure a size of the supervision space for mentioned direction%CrLf%and then restart control. After occurred restart, check the feedback of the mentioned supervision space.
549;24;%4no value axis 7 for %1 monitoring area configured;In the configuration, a value must be configured for the auxiliary axis of the mentioned supervision space. With this robot type and existing installation site, the auxiliary axis must be supervised.;In the configuration file Robotcontrol.cfg, configure a value of the supervision space for the auxiliary axis %CrLf%%CrLf%and then restart control. After occurred restart, check the feedback of the mentioned supervision space.
549;25;%4Bypass and Unselect cannot be evaluated, number of gripper points=%1;Invalid configuration [RC.KINEMATIC:x.Gripper] %CrLf% nrOfVectors = 0%CrLf%This value is inadmissible. If no grippers are defined, the controller cannot monitor any working spaces.;Check configuration and restart control.
550;1;%4Inconsistent feedback of the fixation cylinder handler tool.;The fixation cylinder of the handler tool gives inconsistent feedback, in and out at the same time.%CrLf%Hardware disturbed, Cable break, dirt... ;Check initiator and cabling and exchange where appropriate.
550;2;%4The fixation cylinder of the handler tool has not reached its target position.;- Approach switch acknowledgement defective%CrLf%- Malfunction of the air supply%CrLf%- Mechanical air supply;- Check air supply %CrLf%- Check ease of movement%CrLf%- Check proximity switch feedback
550;3;%4Inconsistent feedback of the swivel drive for the handler tool.;The swivel drive of the handler tool gives inconsistent feedback, more than one position at the same time.%CrLf%Hardware disturbed, Cable break, dirt... ;Check initiator and cabling and exchange where appropriate.
550;4;%4The swivel drive of the handler tool has not reached its target position.;- Approach switch acknowledgement defective%CrLf%- Malfunction of the air supply%CrLf%- Mechanical air supply;- Check air supply %CrLf%- Check ease of movement%CrLf%- Check proximity switch feedback
550;5;%4No feedback of the fixation cylinder for handler tool.;The Initiators (moved In / moved out) are delivering implausible or no feedback.;- Check position of the Swivel drive/fixation cylinder.%CrLf%- Check wiring and Initiators.
550;6;%4Handler tool is not in production positioin (Cylinder moved out, Swivel drive in Centreposition).;At program start of a car body program the handler tool has to be in required position (fixation cylinder moved out and swivel drive in home position).;- Check position of the Swivel drive/fixation cylinder.%CrLf%- Check wiring and Initiators.
550;7;%4The swivel drive of the handler tool has left the cleaning position.;- Approach switch acknowledgement defective%CrLf%- Malfunction of the air supply%CrLf%- Mechanical air supply;- Check air supply %CrLf%- Check ease of movement%CrLf%- Check proximity switch feedback
552;2;%4Failed to create relation to sercos ring ;The reference to the hardware end point "SERCOS" could not be made. The Sercos ring has no symbolic name or another than "SERCOS" in the configuration:%CrLf%[IO.ONBOARD.SLOTPCI:2.FX780A:0.SERCOS:0]%CrLf%name = "SERCOS";Check and correct configuration, then restart control.
