568;6;%4Logged in user has no access to T2 mode ;The user logged in at EcoScreen does not have any authorization for the T2 mode, only instructed specialists have this authorization.;A user with authorization for T 2 mode must log in at EcoScreen.
568;7;%4Log in of user %1 denied ;The maximum number of write-entitled users has been reached (maxLocalWriteSessions).%CrLf%- internal system problem.;Check and correct configuration, then restart control.
568;8;%4Timeout when logging in user %1 ;The login of the mentioned user could not be carried out successfully in the given time.%CrLf%Internal control problem in the communication with TeachView.;Try to log the user in or off again. %CrLf%- If the problem should persist, restart the computer and/or restart ViewServer.%CrLf%- Should the problem should persist, contact the controller supplier.
568;9;%4Failed to log in user %1;The call of an MCU system function failed, internal control error.;Try to log the user in or off again. %CrLf%- If the problem should persist, restart the computer and/or restart ViewServer.%CrLf%- Should the problem should persist, contact the controller supplier.
568;10;%4No OPC user configured in AAd.dat for the user level set in EcoScreen set or for a lower user level;In the user administration, no OPC master user is configured for the user level set by the vision system.;Check user administration and align with configuration of the vision system.
568;11;%4Failed to log off user %1;Error when attempting to log out the current user of TeachView.%CrLf%Internal control problem..;Try to log the user in or off again. %CrLf%- If the problem should persist, restart the computer and/or restart ViewServer.%CrLf%- Should the problem should persist, contact the controller supplier.
568;12;%4Not all the required user for TeachView configured in the file %1, path: %2.;User administration for TeachView is not completely configured in the file AAd.dat.;Copy completely configured AAd.dat from master project to mentioned folder and restart PC.
568;13;%4Configuration %1=%2 is invalid. %3 expected.;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Please check this value in file "services.cfg".
569;2;%4Call of the function McuCreateJob failed ;The call of the MCU function McuCreateJob was not successful. The configured bypass area cannot be controlled.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
569;5;%4No monitoring range defined.;In the configuration no bypass area was parameterized.;None
569;6;%4Failed to map the assigned kinematics ;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Check configuration and restart control.
570;1;%4Invalid drive type or error when reading the drive firmware.;Cannot read drive parameter S0-0030.%CrLf%Drive firmware version is not known to the controller.;Pay attention to further drive errors, contact controller manufacturer where appropriate.
570;2;%4Invalid bus type or error when reading the drive bustype.;Cannot read drive parameter S0-0030.%CrLf%Drive firmware version is not known to the controller.;Pay attention to further drive errors, contact controller manufacturer where appropriate.
571;1;%4Mapping of the assigned kinematics failed ;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Check configuration and restart control.
571;2;%4Drive %1 cannot be saved because it is simulated. ;In the configuration file "IoSercos.cfg" the "driverMode = 3" is selected with the mentioned drive, which means simulation.;In the configuration file -IoSercos.cfg- set the -driverMode = 1- and restart control.
571;3;%4Failed to read list of the data of drive %1 which should be saved. ;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
571;4;%4Failed to read attribute value for parameter %1 of drive %2 ;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
571;5;%4Failed to read name of the parameter %1 of drive %2;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
571;6;%4Failed to read unit of the parameter %1 of drive %2;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
571;7;%4Failed to create folder %1 for the drive parameters which should be saved ;It was attempted to create the indicated directory. This was not possible, however.%CrLf%- Target path reserved%CrLf%- System-dependent refusal of hard disk access%CrLf%- Internal error%CrLf%;Check the indicated path in the Explorer.
571;8;%4Error when writing file %1;It was attempted to create the indicated file. This was not possible, however.%CrLf%- Target file available, but write-protected.%CrLf%- Hard disk access refused for reasons that are inherent in the system ;Check the indicated path in the Explorer.
572;1;%4Failed to map the assigned kinematics;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Check configuration and restart control.
572;2;%4Robot not in brake check position;Robot was not moved into brake test position.%CrLf%Brake test position not configured.;Check robot position.%CrLf%Check configuration of the fixed positions with ProcessBuilder.
572;3;%4Brake check must be executed in %1 hours;Brake test was not carried out in the last 24 hours.%CrLf%Note for customers that brake test must be carried out in x hours,%CrLf%otherwise the drives will be shut down.;Carry out brake test.
572;4;%4No brake check has been carried out for more than 48 hours,;The brake test must be carried out after 48 hours at the latest, this has occurred.;Carry out brake test.
572;5;%4Preliminary movement release by %1 ;User gave the provisional travel release at the teach pendant or at EcoScreen.;None
572;6;%4Request brake check to PLC cannot be set, no access to output %1 ;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped. Different designation of the hardware end points in the Kemro manager and RCU. Input/output was not created in the Kemro manager.  ;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
572;8;%4The automatic brake test of drive %1 has failed. The brake must be grindid-in.;The holding torque of the motor brake is not sufficient.;The motor brake must be grinded-in.
573;1;%4Error when writing the torque S-0-0092 at drive %1;It was attempted to write a parameter to the respective drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
573;2;%4Brake check at drive %1 aborted because drive not switched on;At the beginning of the brake test, the concerned drive was not connected or %CrLf%was switched off during the test.;Turn on drive.
573;3;%4Error when writing %1 command to drive %2;It was attempted to write a parameter to the respective drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
573;4;%4max time for brake check axis %1 exceeded;The brake test could not be ended successfully within the preset time.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
573;5;%4Failed to read result of ATEX brake check of drive %1, parameter %2. ;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, carry out function again where appropriate.
573;6;%4Error in phase %1 during ATEX brake check at drive %2 ;At the specified axis, an error occurred in the mentioned phase of the brake test.;Check control element and drive. For this, also refer to special documentation "TB 132"
573;7;%4ATEX brake check at drive %1 successful ;The ATEX brake test was carried out successfully.;None
573;8;%4Velocity during looping in the brake at axis %1 too high;When grinding in the brake, the speed of the motor must not be too high since otherwise the brake might be damaged. The speed is set in the teach program and is too high.;Set grinding-in speed to a regular value (V25 or V50).
573;9;%4Velocity for grinding in the brake of axis %1 not reached yet;The necessary minimum speed to grind in the motor blocking brake was not reached within the set time.;Set grinding-in speed to a regular value (V25 or V50).
573;10;%4Brake test / -grind in drive %1 not possible, motor is Ex-controlled of the type %2.;Brake test/grinding in cannot be carried out for EX protected motors.;Check control element and drive. For this, also refer to special documentation "TB 132"
573;11;%4 %1: Grinding-in path too short or grinding-in speed too high.;Grinding-in path too short or grinding-in speed too high.;Increase grinding-in path or set grinding-in speed to a regular value (V25 or V50).
573;12;%4Brake grinding is not allowed in T1 mode.;Brake grinding is not allowed in T1 mode.;Please switch to T2 or Hand mode.
574;1;%4Failed to read configuration data of drive parameters, parameter group %1;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration and restart control.
574;2;%4Failed to read scaling factor for parameter %1 of drive %2;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, contact controller manufacturer where appropriate.
574;3;%4Failed to read parameter %1 of drive %2;It was attempted to read a parameter of the drive control element via Sercos, here, errors occurred.%CrLf%Defective optical waveguide or other drive error.;Pay attention to further drive errors, contact controller manufacturer where appropriate.
574;4;%4Failed to switch on drive %1, parameter %2 differs from the configuration;At a drive, an invalid standard parameter record was activated by acknowledging the message UL.;Load original parameter set into the drive.
574;5;%4%1 and/or %2 not configured;Control was stopped due to a fatal error!;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
575;1;%4Not able to get access to all inputs/outputs of the field bus slave;Not all inputs/outputs of the field bus slave could be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware end points in the Kemromanager and RCU.%CrLf%Input/output was not created or several inputs/outputs in the Kemromanager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
575;2;%4Failed to get access to the binary input %1, mapping error;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware endpoint in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input was not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
575;3;%4Failed to get access to the input byte %1, mapping error;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware endpoint in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input was not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
575;4;%4Failed to get access to the input word %1, mapping error;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware endpoint in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input was not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
575;5;%4Failed to get access to the binary output %1, mapping error.;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware endpoint in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input was not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
575;6;%4Failed to get access to the output byte %1, mapping error ;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware endpoint in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input was not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
575;7;%4Failed to get access to the output word %1, mapping error ;The mentioned hardware endpoint of the field bus slave could not be mapped.%CrLf%Different designation of the hardware endpoint in the Kemro manager and RCU.%CrLf%Input was not created in the Kemro manager.;Check configuration with Kemromgr and align with interface documentation,%CrLf%then restart control.
576;1;%4Missing configuration input [RC.Symbols];Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration, possibly recreate, restart control
576;2;%4Missing configuration input for device signal names %1;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration, possibly recreate, restart control
576;3;%4System variable %1 not mapped;Programming error or internal control problem;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
577;1;%4Failed to map the corresponding kinematics ;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Check configuration and restart control.
577;2;%4Tool cannot be detected by light barrier;The light barrier was not interrupted during the programmed movement to the target. Possible causes: %CrLf%- execution of the teach program in the STEP mode%CrLf%- movement wrong or wrong sequence of the macros%CrLf%- sensor signal wrong;Correct teach program and restart program
577;4;%4sensor input '%1' not available;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration and restart control.
577;5;%4Variable %1 not mapped;Programming error or internal control problem;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
577;6;%4Selected direction of measurement %1, is not allowed with configured measuring type = %2;Refer to error text;Either change EcoTalk program so that the measuring direction matches the configuration or change the configuration.
577;8;%4Tool is still in the area of the light barrier;The light barrier remains interrupted during the programmed movement to the target. Possible causes:%CrLf%- Execution of the teach program in STEP mode%CrLf%- Movement wrong or wrong sequence of macros%CrLf%- Sensor signal wrong%CrLf%- Target taught wrong;Correct teach program and restart program
577;9;%4Configuration for the tool measurement faulty. Entry '%1' not existing;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration and restart control.
577;10;%4Tolerance range for ToolMeasure in %1 direction chosen too big (%2), allowed (%3).;In the movement program a tolerance was defined with the command "SETTOLERANCE" which is bigger than allowed.;Correct EcoTalk command according to EcoTalk Doku and reload teach program.
577;11;%4EcoTalk command -SAVETOOL- was executed but no tolerances were set before by -SETTOLERANCE-.;Tolerance for ToolMeasure neigther configured nor set by EcoTalk command.%CrLf%Because of the received correction values inn command -SAVETOOL- can not be verified.;Check logical schedule of movement program according EcoTalk documentation.
577;12;%4Deviation %1 in %2 direction exceeds warning limit %3. Outlet will be locked.;Parameterized permissible warning limit for the tool exceeded.%CrLf%Outlet will be locked.;Check application and release outlet afterwards.%CrLf%Check Tool and change if necessary.
577;13;%4Deviation %1 in %2 direction exceeds warning limit %3.;Parameterized permissible warning limit for the tool exceeded.;Check application and Tool and change if necessary.
577;14;%4The tool correction functionality was configured however without activating the extended interface.;The following parameter has to be activated in the configuration.%CrLf%[RC.KINEMATIC:0.Vision]%CrLf%UseExtendedPLCinterface   = 1;Check configuration and restart control.
577;23;%4Maximum curvature of tool in %1 direction exceeded. Curvature = %2. Exchange nozzle!;Parameterized permissible tolerance for the tool exceeded;Exchange tool
577;27;%4Call of SAVETOOL with invalid measured values;At least one measured value for one of the three traveling directions is invalid;Change teach program so that there are valid measuring rides for all three directions, or check sensor signal or check tool for damage
578;1;%4Incomplete configuration: KINEMATIC:X.TorqueCheck;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration and restart control.
578;2;%4Failed to map system variable %1 for EcoScreen.;Project planning error in robot software.;Rework project planning.
578;3;%4Incomplete configuration: KINEMATIC:X.TorqueCheck;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration and restart control.
578;4;%4Axis number for torque check invalid ;Invalid parameterization.;Check parameterization
578;5;%4Limit value for torque check is outside of the max. motor torque;Invalid parameterization.;Check parameterization
578;6;%4New limit value for torque check: %1 ;User information;None
578;7;%4Torque check already active ;User information;None
578;8;%4Maximum limit in torque check reached ;The monitoring function of the torque monitoring has detected that the parameterized limit was exceeded.;Check whether there is a collision. If no, check parameterization.
578;9;%4Minimum limit in torque check reached ;The monitoring function of the torque monitoring has detected that the parameterized limit was fallen below.;Check whether there is a collision. If no, check parameterization.
578;10;%4Part was not found during torque check ;The monitoring function of the torque monitoring has detected that the part was not caught.;Check whether the part was gripped. If yes, check parameterization.
578;11;%4Torque check has been disabled ;User information;None
578;12;%4Backward movement failed ;Internal control problem.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
578;13;%4Torque observation: Do visual inspection ;A transgression of the parameterized torque was found before.;Check visually, because a transgression of the parameterized torque was found before.
579;2;%4Start of data recording not possible. Recording already started for axis %1 ;In the teach program, the macro TORQUEMONITOR with the parameter StartLogging is called twice consecutively. Only one recording can be started.;Correct teach program and stop preceding recording before the 2nd start of the recording.
579;3;%4No recording was started. No file is created.;The macro TORQUEMONITOR with the parameter StopLogging was called and before no recording with the macro TORQUEMONITOR and the parameter StartLogging was started.;Correct teach program and start the recording with TORQUEMONITOR( StartLogging???  ) before. 
579;4;%4Program error. Recording was started for axis %1 and is supposed to be finished for axis %2 ;The recording was started with the macro TORQUEMONITOR( StartLogging, Axis 1) for e.g. axis 1 and shall be ended with TORQUEMONITOR( StopLogging, Axis 2) for e.g. axis 2. Since the selected axes are different, the results would be saved in a wrong file.;Correct teach program and correct the axis parameter in the macro TORQUEMONITOR( StopLogging??? ).
580;1;%4Phototherm: Unknown error (%1);The phototherm measuring device has received an unknown error code.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
580;9;%4Phototherm: Trigger timeout for chopper modulation  ;The stepping motor of the chopper that modulates the laser was stopped. The measuring software attempts to start the stepping motor again automatically. In most cases, this action is sufficient and the measuring instrument will measure correctly again.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
580;10;%4Phototherm: Calibration file not found ;The calibrating file is not available on the phototherm measuring PC in the directory c:\ps3\caldir1.;Check file or recreate with the aid of PS3.exe. The calibrating file must be entered in the last column of the text file colorlst.da2.
580;15;%4Phototherm: Laser on not detected ;The output signal of the laser that indicates the correct emission is missing. The laser is not ready for use.;The laser is switched off automatically in case of overheating. Check cooling unit (flow, water level, temperature). Check signals for flow, water level and temperature. If cooling unit is ok, restart laser power by means of software. If the error is still pending, the current supply or the laser may be defective. Contact controller supplier.
580;18;%4Phototherm: result file could not be opened for writing.;Another program blocked the file.;Close all programs accessing this file. Acknowledge error. If error occurs again, contact controller supplier.
580;19;%4Phototherm: Amplitude too low ;The reception amplitude is too small for a correct measurement result. The amplifier stage is too low or the laser is off or the film thickness is too small or cable or detector error.;Check amplifier stage and increase where appropriate or turn on laser or check film thickness and/or the measurement points or cable in the teach program and/or check detector or contact controller supplier.
580;20;%4Phototherm: Signal amplitude too high;Signal amplitude is too large for the amplifier (beyond range +- 15V). This leads to an incorrect measurement result. Possible causes are: Wrongly set amplifier stage, detector defective, strong light or heat source in the environment);Set amplifier stage lower or check detector or check environmental conditions (strong light or heat sources) and change where appropriate. If no remedial measure: Contact controller supplier/Phototerm.
580;22;%4Phototherm: program operating in test mode ;During the start of the measurement software, the test mode was activated. In this mode, it is not possible to turn on the laser or to carry out real measurements. The mode is used for the test of the software without measuring instrument.;End the measuring software on the Phototherm measuring PC, deactivate the test mode and restart the measuring software
580;23;%4Phototherm: Error at the current supply of the detector;Missing voltage at the power supply of the detector.;Check cable connections between measuring PC and laser unit. Acknowledge error and if error is still pending, contact controller supplier/Phototherm.
580;24;%4Phototherm: Error at +/- 15V current supply B %;Missing voltage at the power supply B.;Check cable connections between measuring PC and laser unit. Acknowledge error and if error is still pending, contact controller supplier/Phototherm.
580;25;%4Phototherm: Error at +/- 15V current supply A ;Missing voltage at the power supply A.;Check cable connections between measuring PC and laser unit. Acknowledge error and if error is still pending, contact controller supplier/Phototherm.
580;26;%4Phototherm: Error at current supply of the laser ;Missing voltage at the power supply of the laser.;Check cable connections between measuring PC and laser unit. Acknowledge error and if error is still pending, contact controller supplier/Phototherm.
580;27;%4Phototherm: Error at 24 V Relay power supply;Missing voltage at the 24V power supply of the relays.;Check cable connections between measuring PC and laser unit. Acknowledge error and if error is still pending, contact controller supplier/Phototherm.
580;100;%4No configuration found for the Phototherm measuring device;Faulty configuration;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
580;101;%4The Phototherm device is simulated. Inputs are copied from HMI interface. ;In the configuration, the simulation mode is activated.;If real measuring instrument is available, correct configuration.
580;102;%4Phototerm: Measurement series was stopped, but no series was started. ;A series of measurements was stopped with the macro ACTIVATE_PAC(DISABLE), but no series of measurements was started before;Check teach program and adapt.
580;103;%4A single measurement is supposed to be started. No measurement series was started. ;Error in the process. A single measurement was started although no series of measurements was started.;Correct teach program or if the error occurs again, contact controller supplier.
580;104;%4Phototerm: A measurement series was started but the device is not ready or an error is pending. ;Measuring instrument is not ready or an error is pending.;Activate measuring instrument or eliminate error.
580;105;%4Phototerm: A single measurement was started but the device is not ready or an error is pending. ;Measuring instrument is not ready or an error is pending.;Activate measuring instrument or eliminate error.
581;1;%4No laser release from PLC and a measurement sequence is running;While an object is measured, the laser release was dropped%CrLf%- Laser release from PLC is not available%CrLf%;Eliminate error.
581;13;%4Single measurement was started but no measure sequence was started.;Error in the process. A single measurement was started although no series of measurements was started.;Correct teach program or if the error occurs again, contact controller supplier.
581;14;%4A measure sequence is started but a measure sequence is already running.;Error in the teaching program. Error in the teach program. A series of measurements was started twice with ACTIVATE_PAC(OneShot).;Correct teaching program.
581;15;%4Start of measure sequence but measuring device is not in emission mode;A series of measurements is supposed to be started and the measuring instrument is not in the correct operating mode.;Release and turn on measuring instrument.
581;16;%4Macro 'ACTIVATE_PAC' is called and no laser release available.;A series of measurements is supposed to be started, but there is no laser release from the PLC.;Turn on measuring instrument and release in EcoScreen
581;17;%4The software on the Phototherm PC is not ready. The signal 'SoftwareReady' is not set.;The software on the Phototherm PC is not ready. The signal 'SoftwareReady' is missing.;Check or restart software on Phototherm-PC. Cehck signal cables between Phototherm-PC and RPC.
581;101;%4Colorgroup %1 out of range 0 - 32.;The number of the color group is beyond the range.;Correct color assignment in EcoScreen.
581;102;%4PaintChecker: No configuration found.;Configuration error;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
581;103;%4Too many measurement points (Max: %1).;Too many measurement points are defined in the teach program. Internal field limits would be exceeded. Measuring data will be lost.;Correct teach program, contact control manufacturer or increase the constant cMaxNoOfPoints to TRcuPaintChecker.tts.
581;300;%4Error while uploading Measure datas to HMI (Error);File Measure could not be uploaded to HMI;-Check Network connection. Check OPCLink Topic state. Check Paintchecker RPC Server connection state
581;301;%4Error while uploading Measure datas to HMI (Message);File Measure could not be uploaded to HMI;-Check Network connection. Check OPCLink Topic state. Check Paintchecker RPC Server connection state
581;1044;%4%1 could not be mapped.;Internal control problem, programming error or parameterizing error.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
582;1;%4Configuration for VMT-BK faulty.;Error in the configuration or configuration file not available.;Check configuration and restart control.
582;2;%4Failed to map the appendant kinematics ;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
582;3;%4Timeout when sending data (%1);Communication problem between control and VMT BK computer;Get in contact with control supplier.
582;4;%4Timeout when receiving data (%1);Communication problem between control and VMT BK computer;Get in contact with control supplier.
582;5;%4Invalid mode %1;BK_START not possible with this mode. Reserved for extensions.;Correct teach program and restart program
582;6;%4Invalid path %1/%2;For the chosen combination of type and path, there are no adjustment values. An application ride is not possible.;Before the application ride, a measuring ride must be carried out.
582;7;%4Number of points required %1 <> actual %2;The parameter numberOfPoint in the macro BK_FINISH does not agree with the number of the path points and/or measurement points of the path.;Check, correct and reload EcoTalk program between BK_START and BK_FINISH.
582;8;%4Measuring value for point %1 invalid;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;9;%4Collision warning at point %1;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;10;%4Measuring value for point %1 too high;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;11;%4General error at point %1;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;12;%4No correction for point %1;There are no adjustment values for the PointNo in the macro BK_CORR.;Check teach program and/or repeat measuring ride. Restart teach program.
582;13;%4Trigger for point %1 as long as last signal still set;The reaching of a measurement point is signaled to the BK system by setting a bit on the interface. While this bit is being still set, the next measurement point is already supposed to be signaled.;Increase the spatial and/or chronological distance between the measurement points (BK_ACTION and/or BK_ACTION_DIRECT) and restart the program.
582;14;%4Adjustment values beyond tolerance range;The adjustment values of the BK system are absolutely larger than the permissible parameterized limit values.;No application must be carried out on the car body.
582;15;%4Auto path point function not implemented;Function reserved for extensions.;Get in contact with control supplier.
582;16;%4Point number used several times;The point number in the macro BK_CORR was already used.;Check, correct and reload EcoTalk program between BK_START and BK_FINISH.
582;17;%4Not enough adjustment values for the path received;Function reserved for extensions.;Get in contact with control supplier.
582;18;%4Point %1 is not Cartesian;The teach program uses path points between BK_START and BK_FINISH in axis coordinates. These cannot be transmitted to the BK system as path points.;Check teach program and adapt.
582;19;%4Internal error. Index %1 out of range;Programming error or internal control problem;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
582;20;%4BK status not ok;The BK system reports an error status.;Check the status at the BK computer
582;21;%4Failed to map system variable -%1- for EcoScreen.;Programming error or internal control problem;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
582;22;%4Timeout when receiving data (%1);10 seconds after the end of the measurement, not all adjustment values were transferred to the controller yet;Get in contact with control supplier.
582;23;%4TCP/IP connection faulty;The TCP/IP connection to the server located on the vision-pc could not be established;Check wiring. Check TCPIP addresses and ports in the parametrization
582;24;%4The path correction functionality was configured however without activating the extended interface;The following parameter has to be activated in the configuration.%CrLf%[RC.KINEMATIC:0.Vision]%CrLf%UseExtendedPLCinterface   = 1;Check configuration and restart control.
582;25;%4Displacement values out of range.;The adjustment values of the BK system are absolutely larger than the permissible parameterized limit values.;No application must be carried out on the car body.
582;26;%4No access to variable %1 from system _globalvars.tid.;Variable not existing in _globalvars.tid.;Verify if variable is written correctly and restart the robot control
582;28;%4Measuring value for point %1 invalid;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;29;%4Collision warning at point %1;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;30;%4Measuring value for point %1 too high;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
582;31;%4General error at point %1;Status message from the VMT BK system;Inspection of the parameterization at the VMT-BK system
