583;1;%4Failed to map the appendant kinematics.;The attempt to access to the kinematics failed, programming error or internal control problem.;Restart control. Contact control supplier if this should occur repeatedly.
583;2;%4The points P1, P2 and P3 in the macro INIT3DOBJECT do not define any level;The teaching points P1, P2 and P3 are on one line. The calculation of a level from the three points is not possible.;Reteach the points in such a way that a level is defined
583;3;%4sensor input '%1' not available;Configuration error;Check configuration and restart control.
583;4;%4Parameter P%1 = '%2' in the macro %3 is not an object point;The mentioned point is not taught in the object coordinate system (but in axes or in world);Create point in the object coordinate system
583;5;%4The points P1, P2 and P3 in the macro INIT3DOBJECT are almost on a straight line;The teaching points P1, P2 and P3 are approximately on one line. The calculation of the level through the three points is badly conditioned.;Reteach the points in such a way that a level is defined
583;6;%4Macro %1 cannot be used;The macro was called although the corresponding step was not selected in CONFIG3D.;Remove the macro from the teach program or activate the step in CONFIG3D.
583;7;%4Macro %1 used without initialization;The macro was called without having defined the reference values with INIT3DOBJECT before.;Before calling the macro in the teach program, call the macro INIT3DOBJECT.
583;8;%4Macro %1 cannot be carried out before %2;The macro mentioned first was called, although the macro mentioned second was not executed successfully yet.;Change order of execution in the teach program.
583;9;%4Macro %1 measurement point %2 difference to the reference point = %3 too large;Difference between the measurement at the reference car body and the measurement at the current car body is larger than the limit value parameterized in [RC.KINEMATIC:0.ObjMeasure].;Car body cannot be measured and applied any further for safety reasons. Abort program and convey car body out.
583;10;%4Measurement point %1: Sensor does not switch;On the programmed path, no signal comes from the distance sensor;Check whether the sensor is turned on and the distance to the surface is within the switching area.
583;11;%4Macro %1 Measuring point %2 Difference between measuring methods too large: %3. ;The difference between the two methods of measurement (drive and bus system) is larger than the parameterized value [RC.KINEMATIC:0.ObjMeasure].;Car body cannot be measured and applied any further for safety reasons. Abort program and convey car body out.
583;12;%4Outlet is blocked because of a measuring error.;Caliper did not trigger (sensor does not switch ).%CrLf% Difference to the reference point too large. %CrLf% Difference between the methods of measurement too large.;Evaluate concurrent error report.
583;13;%4Error when reading the position data of the drives.;Problem in the communication between control and drive control element.;Acknowledge, in case of repeated occurrence, contact control supplier.
