585;5;%4SmartRay-PC signals an error.;The PC pore detection reports a general error to the robot controller;At the PC pore detection (SmartRay), search for the error cause 
585;6;%4The maximum deviation from the path is too large.;The path regulation causes a deviation from the programmed paths that is larger than the parameterized permissible value in [RC.KINEMATIC:0.SmartRay] MaxCorrVal.;Abort program. Move robot into the home position in T1/T2.
585;7;%4Seam lost while running the path search.;During the search ride, the sensor reports that the seam is no more in the sensor's visibility field.;Reteach the search ride 
585;8;%4Start of the seam check too late.;When the seam check is started, the seam is already in the sensors visibility field. Maybe the seam cannot be checked completely.;Adapt teach program. The start of the seam check must occur earlier on the path.
585;9;%4End of the seam check too early.;When the seam check is ended, the seam xxx is still in the sensors visibility field. Maybe the seam cannot be checked completely.;Adapt teach program. The start of the seam check must occur later on the path.
585;10;%4Leap in sensor value %1 %2;The difference between the sensor values of two successive control times exceeds the parameterized limit value.;End teach program. If the error occurs repeatedly, contact the control manufacturer.
